WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Downloaded @ subs4free.club


00:00:49.618 --> 00:00:52.314
BoY:
For those of you out there
less experienced than me...


00:00:52.421 --> 00:00:54.389
let me tell you something
about girls.


00:00:55.891 --> 00:00:57.859
They're basically gross.


00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:00.292
See, this is pretty much
black-and-white...


00:01:00.396 --> 00:01:01.920
from where I'm standing.


00:01:02.031 --> 00:01:03.726
Used to be, back in the day...


00:01:03.832 --> 00:01:05.857
maybe fiirst or second grade...


00:01:05.968 --> 00:01:07.993
popular wisdom was
they gave you cooties.


00:01:08.103 --> 00:01:09.229
Cooties?


00:01:09.338 --> 00:01:12.205
She touched me! Cooties!


00:01:12.308 --> 00:01:13.434
Don't touch me!


00:01:13.542 --> 00:01:16.670
Cooties!
He has cooties!


00:01:16.779 --> 00:01:19.771
We didn't know what cooties
were exactly.


00:01:19.882 --> 00:01:23.318
But the general feeling was,
if a girl touched you...


00:01:23.419 --> 00:01:25.444
some very, very bad things
were gonna happen.


00:01:27.656 --> 00:01:30.216
( girls scream )


00:01:35.331 --> 00:01:36.992
How right we were.


00:01:37.099 --> 00:01:38.088
( retching )


00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:39.497
This is me now.


00:01:39.601 --> 00:01:41.569
I've been in love for
two-and-a-half weeks...


00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:46.164
and it's a pain I wouldn't wish
on my worst enemies.


00:01:46.275 --> 00:01:47.401
( sobbing )


00:01:47.509 --> 00:01:49.136
I'm not going
to dress this up pretty.


00:01:49.244 --> 00:01:50.711
just about everything I know
about women...


00:01:50.813 --> 00:01:54.579
love, and the birds
and the frickin'bees...


00:01:54.683 --> 00:01:56.048
I've learned in the past


00:01:56.151 --> 00:01:57.209
two-and-a-half weeks.


00:01:57.319 --> 00:01:58.877
But, when
you're ten years old...


00:01:58.988 --> 00:02:01.047
( wailing ):
Rosemary...!


00:02:01.156 --> 00:02:03.784
...two-and-a-half weeks
can be a lifetime.


00:02:03.892 --> 00:02:07.453
( pop )


00:02:34.223 --> 00:02:38.216
( continues )


00:03:02.151 --> 00:03:04.483
( continues )


00:03:19.868 --> 00:03:21.301
( song ends )


00:03:21.403 --> 00:03:23.963
BoY:
okay, here's the deal.


00:03:24.073 --> 00:03:26.268
If you came to hear some
great New York love story...


00:03:26.375 --> 00:03:27.364
keep walkin;


00:03:27.476 --> 00:03:28.875
You want a real love story?


00:03:28.977 --> 00:03:30.410
I'll tell you a real one.


00:03:30.579 --> 00:03:35.141
My parents. Camp Annawanna.
Catskill Mountains, 1 984.


00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:40.153
My father was 1 9,
and a star sports counselor.


00:03:40.255 --> 00:03:41.552
My mom was a CIT.


00:03:41.657 --> 00:03:44.057
People say she reminded
them of Sissy Spacek.


00:03:46.395 --> 00:03:49.887
What happened under
that harvest moon that summer...


00:03:49.998 --> 00:03:52.159
that's the stuff oflegend.


00:03:52.267 --> 00:03:54.997
In my family, it's what
we like to refer to as


00:03:55.104 --> 00:03:58.232
ancient history.


00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:00.205
These days, my dad's


00:04:00.309 --> 00:04:02.436
sleeping on the couch.


00:04:02.544 --> 00:04:03.670
Due to this unusual quirk


00:04:03.779 --> 00:04:05.178
in the New York State
divorce code...


00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:08.511
Neither one of my parents
could move out of our apartment


00:04:08.617 --> 00:04:12.713
until their settlement is
signed, sealed and delivered.


00:04:12.821 --> 00:04:15.289
Needless to say,
it doesn't make for


00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:17.415
the greatest living
environment.


00:04:17.526 --> 00:04:18.857
Did you drink my Pepsi?


00:04:18.961 --> 00:04:20.155
It was my Pepsi.


00:04:20.262 --> 00:04:21.627
It had my name on it.


00:04:21.730 --> 00:04:23.288
Especially since my mom's


00:04:23.398 --> 00:04:25.025
- ( phone rings )
- recently decided to start dating again.


00:04:25.134 --> 00:04:27.125
Hello.


00:04:27.236 --> 00:04:28.464
MAN:
Leslie.


00:04:28.570 --> 00:04:30.128
Is there anYThing worse


00:04:30.239 --> 00:04:31.968
than being mistaken
for your mother?


00:04:32.074 --> 00:04:33.701
No, this is Gabe.


00:04:33.809 --> 00:04:35.208
Hey, sorry, big guy.


00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:36.470
You two sound so much alike.


00:04:36.578 --> 00:04:38.409
Is your mom around?
This is Ronny.


00:04:38.514 --> 00:04:42.575
LESLI E:
Uh, I've got it, honey.
You can hang up.


00:04:42.684 --> 00:04:46.518
Now that's a real love story.


00:04:46.622 --> 00:04:49.955
This much I know fiirsthand-
love ends.


00:04:50.058 --> 00:04:51.218
You want proof?.


00:04:51.326 --> 00:04:53.794
Check out my parents'
refrigerator.


00:04:53.896 --> 00:04:54.920
( crying )


00:04:55.030 --> 00:04:56.429
Why did I ever have to discover


00:04:56.532 --> 00:05:00.127
this ridiculous pain
inside of me?


00:05:00.235 --> 00:05:02.999
Because two and a half
weeks ago...


00:05:03.105 --> 00:05:05.630
before all this love nonsense-


00:05:05.741 --> 00:05:08.107
and I'm notjust saying
this either-


00:05:08.210 --> 00:05:10.178
now, before all this,
I was happy.


00:05:10.279 --> 00:05:11.246
( sobbing ):
No!


00:05:11.346 --> 00:05:12.870
Truly happy.


00:05:12.981 --> 00:05:15.074
- ( playing dixieland )
- I'm serious.


00:05:15.184 --> 00:05:17.482
My life was fiilled with song...


00:05:17.586 --> 00:05:19.986
and sport...


00:05:20.088 --> 00:05:21.885
and constant adventure.


00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:24.424
( tires squealing
on video game )


00:05:24.526 --> 00:05:27.290
oh, Rosemary.


00:05:27.396 --> 00:05:30.490
Rosemary, Rosemary, Rosemary.


00:05:30.599 --> 00:05:32.567
Why did you ever have
to come into my life?


00:05:32.668 --> 00:05:34.932
Who am I kidding?


00:05:35.037 --> 00:05:39.030
She's been in my life
for as long as I can remember.


00:05:39.141 --> 00:05:41.609
For one little stretch there,
during kindergarten...


00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:42.904
( children laughing )


00:05:43.011 --> 00:05:44.672
...you might even say
we were friends.


00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:46.304
What are you kids
doing under there?


00:05:50.085 --> 00:05:52.019
That was before fiirst grade...


00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:53.985
and the Iron Curtain came down.


00:05:54.089 --> 00:05:55.750
Girls on one side...


00:05:55.857 --> 00:05:57.654
boys on the other.


00:06:00.829 --> 00:06:02.797
oh, she was still there,
of course.


00:06:02.898 --> 00:06:04.889
I have the class pictures
to prove it.


00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:07.491
I just didn't see her.


00:06:07.603 --> 00:06:11.835
I lived in a world of men.


00:06:11.940 --> 00:06:13.305
So, who wants to
go to Duane Reade?


00:06:13.408 --> 00:06:15.808
Man, I am not helping you
steal Kit-Kats again, Max.


00:06:15.911 --> 00:06:17.344
MAN:
Whoa, whoa, whoa!
Watch it!


00:06:17.446 --> 00:06:18.413
But you got no
trouble eating


00:06:18.513 --> 00:06:20.538
the candy I provide
for ya, do ya?


00:06:20.649 --> 00:06:22.981
I'm not doin' look-out.
I'm sorry, guys.


00:06:23.085 --> 00:06:25.178
Hey, guys, it's 5:00.
I gotta roll.


00:06:25.287 --> 00:06:26.652
I thought we were
gonna shoot some 21 ?


00:06:26.755 --> 00:06:28.689
No, I'm meeting my dad
for football practice.


00:06:28.790 --> 00:06:30.758
See you guys later.


00:06:30.859 --> 00:06:32.724
MAX:
The two of you are
so nuts, man.


00:06:32.828 --> 00:06:35.160
See, my father and I
have this sort of plan.


00:06:35.264 --> 00:06:38.995
- I'm gonna be the Tiger Woods
of the placekicking world.
- Nice! Nice!


00:06:39.101 --> 00:06:41.126
- Yeah!
- And he's gonna be my Earl.


00:06:41.236 --> 00:06:42.168
See what I'm saying.


00:06:42.271 --> 00:06:44.136
If you dedicate yourself
to one goal...


00:06:44.239 --> 00:06:46.230
and one goal only,
at a ridiculously young age...


00:06:46.341 --> 00:06:48.206
history has taught us
we can achieve anything, champ.


00:06:48.310 --> 00:06:49.208
Get back there.


00:06:49.311 --> 00:06:50.300
one, two, three, four...


00:06:50.412 --> 00:06:51.572
You see, before
Rosemary Telesco...


00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:53.648
- Nice and easy.
- I had a very fulfiilling life.


00:06:53.749 --> 00:06:54.681
Nice.


00:06:54.783 --> 00:06:56.614
oh, how'd it get so late?


00:06:56.718 --> 00:06:58.913
Your mother's going to have
dinner waiting for you.


00:06:59.021 --> 00:07:00.818
What do you say
we stop by Patsy's


00:07:00.922 --> 00:07:02.184
and get a couple of slices?


00:07:02.291 --> 00:07:03.815
Can I take karate?


00:07:03.925 --> 00:07:04.949
Karate?


00:07:05.060 --> 00:07:06.527
It's a martial art.


00:07:06.628 --> 00:07:08.459
What does karate have to
do with placekicking?


00:07:08.563 --> 00:07:09.757
I don't know.
It can't hurt.


00:07:09.865 --> 00:07:10.889
Well, how much is it?


00:07:10.999 --> 00:07:12.091
I can?


00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:14.327
If it doesn't cost
me an arm and a leg.


00:07:14.436 --> 00:07:16.495
It might help your
flexibility- sure.


00:07:16.605 --> 00:07:18.095
Mistake number one
was ever taking


00:07:18.206 --> 00:07:19.867
that godforsaken class.


00:07:19.975 --> 00:07:22.603
TEACHER:
Karate is not
about strength.


00:07:26.648 --> 00:07:28.582
It's about skill.
It's about focus.


00:07:28.684 --> 00:07:30.845
( door opens, bell dings )


00:07:30.952 --> 00:07:32.283
It's an art
of determination.


00:07:32.387 --> 00:07:34.753
When she showed up
that fiirst day...


00:07:34.856 --> 00:07:36.881
Sorry, my tap
class ran late.


00:07:36.992 --> 00:07:38.687
I was actually kind of glad,
you know?


00:07:38.794 --> 00:07:41.957
A familiar face and all that.


00:07:43.265 --> 00:07:45.062
I didn't know anybody else


00:07:45.167 --> 00:07:47.226
in the class.


00:07:50.639 --> 00:07:53.039
If you can master
the art of karate...


00:07:53.141 --> 00:07:55.507
you can master anything.


00:07:55.610 --> 00:07:57.305
Come on. Hai.!


00:07:58.914 --> 00:08:03.613
( teacher shouts instruction,
class shouts response )


00:08:07.422 --> 00:08:08.889
You're each going to progress
through this course


00:08:08.990 --> 00:08:10.480
at your own pace.


00:08:10.592 --> 00:08:14.790
Those of you who pass the test
to get your yellow belts...


00:08:14.896 --> 00:08:15.794
will be given yellow.


00:08:15.897 --> 00:08:19.924
Those who pass red, red.


00:08:20.035 --> 00:08:24.199
It's about finding
your personal best.


00:08:24.306 --> 00:08:26.103
Come on! Hai.!


00:08:27.576 --> 00:08:29.339
I want you to pair up.


00:08:29.444 --> 00:08:32.174
Everyone gets
a sparring partner.


00:08:34.349 --> 00:08:35.873
oh, the painful dance
of pairing up.


00:08:38.286 --> 00:08:39.810
20 seconds of pure torture.


00:08:45.761 --> 00:08:48.321
Now, I didn't want a girl
for a sparring partner.


00:08:48.430 --> 00:08:49.556
Would you?


00:08:49.664 --> 00:08:51.256
Hey.
Hey.


00:08:51.366 --> 00:08:52.526
( groans quietly )


00:08:52.634 --> 00:08:53.862
okay...


00:08:53.969 --> 00:08:55.266
Ki-yah!


00:08:55.370 --> 00:08:58.305
Let me tell you something
about Rosemary Telesco.


00:08:58.407 --> 00:09:00.500
Rosemary wasn't the prettiest
girl in our class.


00:09:00.609 --> 00:09:02.008
That was Madison Shaw.


00:09:02.110 --> 00:09:04.010
And she wasn't the second
prettiest, either.


00:09:04.112 --> 00:09:05.306
That was Vanessa Muir.


00:09:05.414 --> 00:09:07.678
No, Rosemary was third.


00:09:07.783 --> 00:09:09.774
But boy, could that
girl do karate.


00:09:14.089 --> 00:09:15.181
Ki-yah!


00:09:15.290 --> 00:09:16.621
BoY ( in distance ):
Ki-yah!


00:09:16.725 --> 00:09:17.692
TEACHER:
Keep it tight.


00:09:21.630 --> 00:09:23.825
Don't get the wrong idea.


00:09:23.932 --> 00:09:25.923
We weren't really friends.


00:09:26.034 --> 00:09:28.901
We werejust karate friends.


00:09:29.004 --> 00:09:31.234
Back at school, nothing
changed, of course.


00:09:31.339 --> 00:09:33.136
As far as the rest of the world


00:09:33.241 --> 00:09:34.970
was concerned, the real world...


00:09:35.076 --> 00:09:37.544
that Iron Curtain was
still solid.


00:09:40.749 --> 00:09:42.307
But, when we put
on those white robes...


00:09:42.417 --> 00:09:43.975
we could see past
our many differences


00:09:44.085 --> 00:09:46.349
and fiight like equals.


00:09:46.455 --> 00:09:47.444
Ki-yah!


00:09:47.556 --> 00:09:51.117
There was just
one tiny problem.


00:09:51.226 --> 00:09:53.660
I pretty much sucked at karate.


00:09:53.762 --> 00:09:55.320
Ki-yah!


00:09:57.466 --> 00:10:00.993
We all congratulate
Rosemary Telesco


00:10:01.102 --> 00:10:02.569
on being the first
in the class


00:10:02.671 --> 00:10:04.298
to earn her yellow belt.


00:10:04.406 --> 00:10:06.135
Thank you very much.


00:10:06.241 --> 00:10:07.765
( speaking Japanese )


00:10:07.876 --> 00:10:09.434
( repeating Japanese phrase )


00:10:09.544 --> 00:10:11.011
Talk about an assault
to everything


00:10:11.112 --> 00:10:12.238
I knew about the world.


00:10:12.347 --> 00:10:13.837
RoSEMARY:
Girls mature faster than boys.


00:10:13.949 --> 00:10:14.973
That's completely made up.


00:10:15.083 --> 00:10:16.607
Boys are so much
more mature than girls.


00:10:16.718 --> 00:10:18.117
This isn't a matter
of opinion, Gabe.


00:10:18.220 --> 00:10:19.312
There were studies.


00:10:19.421 --> 00:10:21.548
Girls speak first,
they walk first.


00:10:21.656 --> 00:10:23.556
I see it in my little
sister's class.


00:10:23.658 --> 00:10:25.125
The boys her age
all seem retarded.


00:10:25.227 --> 00:10:27.195
There's absolutely no reason
I shouldn't be able


00:10:27.295 --> 00:10:29.263
to get my yellow belt
in just a week.


00:10:29.364 --> 00:10:30.626
You don't take
it seriously.


00:10:30.732 --> 00:10:31.824
I take it seriously.


00:10:31.933 --> 00:10:33.059
You're not focused.


00:10:33.168 --> 00:10:35.159
You think you're
this natural.


00:10:35.270 --> 00:10:36.202
You don't practice.


00:10:36.304 --> 00:10:37.498
I practice.


00:10:37.606 --> 00:10:38.732
When?
All the time.


00:10:38.840 --> 00:10:40.501
You should practice
with me.


00:10:40.609 --> 00:10:41.541
You'd get better.


00:10:41.643 --> 00:10:42.735
Fine. Let's practice.


00:10:42.844 --> 00:10:43.776
Name the time.


00:10:43.879 --> 00:10:45.039
I don't care.
This afternoon.


00:10:45.146 --> 00:10:46.875
- Fine.
- Great.


00:10:46.982 --> 00:10:48.449
oh, I forgot.


00:10:48.550 --> 00:10:50.518
I have this one errand.


00:10:50.619 --> 00:10:52.109
I'm supposed to be
this flower girl


00:10:52.220 --> 00:10:53.244
in a couple of weeks.


00:10:53.355 --> 00:10:54.481
And I have this fitting.


00:10:54.589 --> 00:10:56.147
But, it's going to be,
like, five minutes.


00:10:56.258 --> 00:10:57.190
I promise.


00:10:57.292 --> 00:10:59.920
GABE:
Classic female move.


00:11:00.028 --> 00:11:01.393
The bait-and-switch.


00:11:01.496 --> 00:11:02.485
My mother's tricked me


00:11:02.597 --> 00:11:06.055
into many a shoe store
with that one.


00:11:06.167 --> 00:11:09.136
Is there anYThing worse
than dress shopping?


00:11:09.237 --> 00:11:10.363
I'm serious.


00:11:10.472 --> 00:11:12.406
I would rather have
my toenails peeled off...


00:11:12.507 --> 00:11:13.735
one by one, with pliers...


00:11:13.842 --> 00:11:16.174
than spend fiive minutes
in a dress store.


00:11:18.880 --> 00:11:20.472
Boo.


00:11:27.789 --> 00:11:31.657
( heart beating
gradually faster )


00:11:33.261 --> 00:11:37.129
okay, what's going on here?


00:11:37.232 --> 00:11:38.961
What the heck is this?


00:11:39.067 --> 00:11:40.534
oh, my God.


00:11:40.635 --> 00:11:44.594
What's this feeling
in the pit of my stomach?


00:11:44.706 --> 00:11:47.436
Who is this... this...


00:11:47.542 --> 00:11:50.875
amazing creature before me?


00:11:50.979 --> 00:11:53.277
What do you think?


00:11:53.381 --> 00:11:57.681
You are going to be the
prettiest flower girl there.


00:11:59.821 --> 00:12:02.881
I'm definitely going
to be the oldest one.


00:12:03.024 --> 00:12:05.322
( squeaking ):
Who...


00:12:05.427 --> 00:12:07.327
( clears throat )
Um, who's getting married?


00:12:07.429 --> 00:12:09.056
My mom's sister.


00:12:09.164 --> 00:12:11.962
oh, cool.


00:12:12.067 --> 00:12:13.398
It's kind of weird...


00:12:13.501 --> 00:12:16.561
'cause she's, like,
seven months pregnant.


00:12:16.671 --> 00:12:19.105
In that one moment...


00:12:19.207 --> 00:12:21.107
Rosemary Telesco leaped
past Vanessa Muir...


00:12:21.209 --> 00:12:23.370
past Madison Shaw.


00:12:23.478 --> 00:12:28.882
I look at Rosemary
andjust felt so, um, confused.


00:12:28.984 --> 00:12:30.417
She's a girl.


00:12:30.518 --> 00:12:32.486
I'm supposed to despise girls...


00:12:32.587 --> 00:12:34.248
not feel nervous
talking to one.


00:12:34.356 --> 00:12:35.880
Not be all tongue-tied.


00:12:35.991 --> 00:12:37.982
I mean, this was
Rosemary Telesco.


00:12:38.093 --> 00:12:39.685
I knew her since kindergarten.


00:12:39.794 --> 00:12:41.523
Whoa!


00:12:41.630 --> 00:12:42.790
Just...just
a little rock.


00:12:42.897 --> 00:12:44.262
I mean, it's gonna
to be fine.


00:12:44.366 --> 00:12:45.924
I'm just gonna...
grab my scooter...


00:12:46.034 --> 00:12:47.433
I'm really cool.
Honestly.


00:12:51.840 --> 00:12:55.332
As she took me to practice
karate at her place...


00:12:55.443 --> 00:12:57.843
one thing became clear.


00:12:57.946 --> 00:12:59.811
Rosemary went to PS 87


00:12:59.914 --> 00:13:02.906
because her parents believed
in public education.


00:13:03.018 --> 00:13:04.576
See, believing
in public education


00:13:04.686 --> 00:13:08.884
wasn't really a luxury
my family could afford.


00:13:08.990 --> 00:13:09.979
( horse neighs )


00:13:10.091 --> 00:13:12.616
Don't go to Taos...
not without me.


00:13:12.727 --> 00:13:14.524
Mr. and Mrs. Telesco,
her parents.


00:13:14.629 --> 00:13:17.393
They, liked, starred
in this soap opera, Santa Fe...


00:13:17.499 --> 00:13:19.433
that's on, like, every day.


00:13:19.534 --> 00:13:21.263
So you know
they had a few bucks.


00:13:21.369 --> 00:13:22.427
oh, look at that.


00:13:22.537 --> 00:13:23.697
You see that?


00:13:23.805 --> 00:13:25.932
I knew your folks were going
to keep 'em together.


00:13:26.041 --> 00:13:27.065
Didn't I say it?


00:13:27.175 --> 00:13:28.403
Let's go practice
in my bedroom.


00:13:28.510 --> 00:13:29.943
okay.


00:13:30.045 --> 00:13:31.637
WoMAN ( on TV):
What do you think
I'm going to say?


00:13:31.746 --> 00:13:32.644
oh, come on.


00:13:32.747 --> 00:13:34.305
He is no good for you!


00:13:34.416 --> 00:13:35.576
Get back in the truck!


00:13:35.684 --> 00:13:39.142
Ifkarate's all about focus...


00:13:39.254 --> 00:13:40.585
Good one.


00:13:40.689 --> 00:13:42.987
...my focus was all over
that pink room.


00:13:43.091 --> 00:13:44.456
I mean, there I was...


00:13:44.559 --> 00:13:45.685
Ki-yah!


00:13:45.794 --> 00:13:47.819
...in the inner sanctum,
alone with her.


00:13:47.929 --> 00:13:49.521
Ki-yah!


00:13:49.631 --> 00:13:51.064
Smelling her smell.


00:13:51.166 --> 00:13:52.133
( sniffs )


00:13:52.233 --> 00:13:54.929
What is that, strawberry?


00:13:55.036 --> 00:13:57.561
So what made you
take karate?


00:13:57.672 --> 00:13:59.230
Uh, made me?!


00:13:59.340 --> 00:14:00.807
Daryl Kitzens.


00:14:00.909 --> 00:14:02.843
Daryl Kitzens made
you take karate?


00:14:02.944 --> 00:14:04.343
Yeah, have you seen the guy?


00:14:04.446 --> 00:14:05.435
He's insane.


00:14:05.547 --> 00:14:07.777
Daryl Kitzens is
without a doubt


00:14:07.882 --> 00:14:09.975
the scariest kid
in the Upper West Side.


00:14:10.085 --> 00:14:11.814
- Ugh!
- He's a fiifth grader...


00:14:11.920 --> 00:14:13.410
but he's supposed to be
in seventh.


00:14:13.521 --> 00:14:14.647
He is a giant.


00:14:14.756 --> 00:14:18.021
Held back two grades
out ofhis fiirst fiive.


00:14:18.126 --> 00:14:19.650
At the rate he's going,
he'll graduate


00:14:19.761 --> 00:14:21.285
from high school at the age 2 7.


00:14:21.396 --> 00:14:23.193
And he'll have terrorized
an entire generation


00:14:23.298 --> 00:14:24.458
of Upper West Siders.


00:14:25.100 --> 00:14:27.261
( grunts )


00:14:27.368 --> 00:14:29.359
Are you afraid he's going
to beat you up?


00:14:29.471 --> 00:14:31.803
No, no, no, no.
of course not.


00:14:31.906 --> 00:14:33.771
I just, you know,
want to be ready


00:14:33.875 --> 00:14:36.002
when that day comes, you know.


00:14:36.111 --> 00:14:38.272
Who was I kidding?
I was petrified.


00:14:38.379 --> 00:14:41.109
Kitzens hangs out a lot
in front of the subway station


00:14:41.216 --> 00:14:44.617
on 7 2nd & Broadway.


00:14:44.719 --> 00:14:47.984
I haven't walked past
that corner since october.


00:14:48.089 --> 00:14:49.681
Well, we should practice more.


00:14:49.791 --> 00:14:51.816
Yeah, sure. Let's go.


00:14:51.926 --> 00:14:54.451
We need to start working
on those maneuvers he taught us.


00:14:54.562 --> 00:14:56.655
Well, I kind of meant
some other time.


00:14:56.765 --> 00:14:57.993
It's getting kind of late.


00:14:58.099 --> 00:14:59.157
( laughs ):
oh.


00:14:59.267 --> 00:15:00.427
Yeah, that sounds great.


00:15:00.535 --> 00:15:02.799
Uh, it's getting kind
of late anyway, so...


00:15:02.904 --> 00:15:04.303
Yeah.


00:15:04.405 --> 00:15:07.340
How could I have said that?


00:15:07.442 --> 00:15:08.704
okay,just shake it off.


00:15:08.810 --> 00:15:10.175
Keep it together.


00:15:10.278 --> 00:15:11.176
( thud )


00:15:11.279 --> 00:15:12.211
Are you okay?


00:15:12.313 --> 00:15:13.746
That's the, uh, the-the door.


00:15:16.151 --> 00:15:18.346
Look at her.


00:15:18.453 --> 00:15:20.580
Living this perfect life
up here.


00:15:20.688 --> 00:15:22.781
With a view of the park
and everything.


00:15:22.891 --> 00:15:24.518
Yet, she's so humble.


00:15:24.626 --> 00:15:25.957
Suddenly...


00:15:26.060 --> 00:15:28.995
Rosemary's whole world
seemed very attractive to me.


00:15:29.097 --> 00:15:31.156
Her parents,
with all their success...


00:15:31.266 --> 00:15:33.700
the nanny who's been with her
since she was born...


00:15:33.802 --> 00:15:35.702
and the adopted
three-year-old sister...


00:15:35.804 --> 00:15:38.102
rescued from an orphanage
in Beijing.


00:15:38.206 --> 00:15:39.571
And me.


00:15:39.674 --> 00:15:41.938
My family's on a one-way ticket
to TheJerry Springer Show.


00:15:42.043 --> 00:15:44.102
- Hi.
- Hi.


00:15:44.212 --> 00:15:46.077
Um, is Leslie around?


00:15:46.181 --> 00:15:47.409
Uh, yeah.


00:15:47.515 --> 00:15:49.813
ADAM:
Les, your date's here!


00:15:52.687 --> 00:15:53.949
She's coming.
I'm her...


00:15:54.055 --> 00:15:56.751
( clears throat ):
...husband.


00:15:56.858 --> 00:15:58.621
( banging and blurping
on video game )


00:15:58.726 --> 00:16:01.559
only 20 more minutes
of video, okay, hon?


00:16:01.663 --> 00:16:02.595
Bedtime soon.


00:16:02.697 --> 00:16:03.595
All right.


00:16:03.698 --> 00:16:04.892
Good night.


00:16:04.999 --> 00:16:06.591
( Adam clears throat )


00:16:06.701 --> 00:16:07.861
( soft chuckle )


00:16:07.969 --> 00:16:09.561
Adam, Ronny.
Ronny, Adam.


00:16:09.671 --> 00:16:11.468
- You guys met?
- Yeah, yeah, we met. At the door.


00:16:11.573 --> 00:16:13.200
- ( mutters )
- okay, good. Shall we, uh... Let's...


00:16:13.308 --> 00:16:15.299
GABE:
See this divorce thing...


00:16:15.410 --> 00:16:16.377
You guys have fun.
Thank you.


00:16:16.477 --> 00:16:17.671
okay.


00:16:17.779 --> 00:16:19.838
...it's a very difficult
situation for everyone.


00:16:19.948 --> 00:16:21.882
This isn't anybody's
fault, you know.


00:16:21.983 --> 00:16:23.473
It's not anybody's fault.


00:16:23.585 --> 00:16:27.214
It's just that
your father and I


00:16:27.322 --> 00:16:28.983
are a lot more different
than we thought.


00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:30.853
They'rejust very
different people.


00:16:30.959 --> 00:16:32.392
( crying )


00:16:32.493 --> 00:16:33.858
Even though
I was just nine and a half...


00:16:33.962 --> 00:16:37.454
I totally took it like a man.


00:16:37.565 --> 00:16:40.329
Now, I'm not saying
I'm some latch-key kid.


00:16:40.435 --> 00:16:42.266
I mean, I don't want
to make it seem


00:16:42.370 --> 00:16:43.632
like my parents are
irresponsible, either.


00:16:43.738 --> 00:16:44.898
But, for a year now...


00:16:45.006 --> 00:16:47.270
I've been able
to roam the city.


00:16:47.375 --> 00:16:50.776
Well, okay...


00:16:50.879 --> 00:16:54.906
not really the city-
nine square blocks.


00:16:55.016 --> 00:16:56.984
The planetarium to the north...


00:16:57.085 --> 00:16:59.246
Riverside Park to the west...


00:16:59.354 --> 00:17:02.448
Central Park to the east
and 7 2nd Street to the south.


00:17:02.557 --> 00:17:06.823
( alternative )


00:17:06.928 --> 00:17:09.158
In those blocks,
I own this town.


00:17:18.907 --> 00:17:21.501
( continues )


00:17:21.609 --> 00:17:22.769
Rosemary lived on 8 1 st Street


00:17:22.877 --> 00:17:27.507
near the park, a few yards
north of my territory.


00:17:27.615 --> 00:17:29.810
When I started,you know...


00:17:29.918 --> 00:17:31.852
casually riding
past her building...


00:17:31.953 --> 00:17:34.217
I was heading
into some uncharted waters.


00:17:34.322 --> 00:17:39.851
( continues )


00:17:39.961 --> 00:17:41.428
It was summer break.


00:17:41.529 --> 00:17:43.292
our next karate class wasn't
for three days.


00:17:43.398 --> 00:17:45.832
Do you know
how many Telescos there are


00:17:45.934 --> 00:17:48.835
in the Manhattan phone book?
Two.


00:17:48.937 --> 00:17:50.598
- ( phone ringing )
- Telesco's.


00:17:50.705 --> 00:17:52.002
one's a butcher shop


00:17:52.106 --> 00:17:53.733
down in the Village.


00:17:53.841 --> 00:17:54.865
Rosemary?


00:17:54.976 --> 00:17:58.036
Nah, there's no
Rosemary here.


00:17:58.146 --> 00:17:59.477
And trust me...


00:17:59.580 --> 00:18:00.842
( buzzing ):
This is Frank.


00:18:00.949 --> 00:18:03.179
...the other was
not her, either.


00:18:03.284 --> 00:18:06.310
Hi. Is, uh, R-Rosemary there?


00:18:06.421 --> 00:18:09.015
You're the kid that called
a half an hour ago.


00:18:09.123 --> 00:18:11.353
What was I to do...


00:18:11.459 --> 00:18:15.020
except loiter and hope.


00:18:19.767 --> 00:18:22.565
Uh-oh, her doorman's
looking at me.


00:18:26.374 --> 00:18:29.070
oh, my God, there she is.


00:18:29.177 --> 00:18:31.702
I didn't have
a contingency plan for if


00:18:31.813 --> 00:18:33.212
I actually saw her.


00:18:33.314 --> 00:18:34.838
just go up to her.


00:18:34.949 --> 00:18:38.112
Go, go. Say hi to her.


00:18:38.219 --> 00:18:40.813
( song ends with needle scratching )


00:18:40.922 --> 00:18:43.413
She looked so busy.
I-I'll talk to her another day.


00:18:43.524 --> 00:18:45.890
Coward. You fool.
How could you be so weak?


00:18:45.994 --> 00:18:48.428
I-I'm not weak. I'm only human.


00:18:48.529 --> 00:18:50.360
What was I going to say?
I was in the neighborhood?


00:18:50.465 --> 00:18:51.557
That's pathetic.


00:18:51.666 --> 00:18:53.395
No,you're weak,
and you're pathetic...


00:18:53.501 --> 00:18:55.594
and you're going to be alone
your entire life.


00:18:55.703 --> 00:18:57.102
Who cares?


00:18:57.205 --> 00:18:59.230
I'd rather be alone than endure
this misery and torment.


00:19:00.508 --> 00:19:01.975
Whoa!
ooh!


00:19:03.177 --> 00:19:04.405
Hey, watch it, child!


00:19:04.512 --> 00:19:05.570
Gabe?


00:19:05.680 --> 00:19:08.672
oh, uh, hi.


00:19:08.783 --> 00:19:09.772
How's-How's it going?


00:19:09.884 --> 00:19:11.476
( stammering ):
I was just, you know...


00:19:11.586 --> 00:19:12.780
in the neighborhood.


00:19:12.887 --> 00:19:14.821
Don't you live
in the neighborhood?


00:19:14.922 --> 00:19:18.085
Well, 73rd & West End.


00:19:18.192 --> 00:19:22.060
I-I guess it sort of depends on
how the neighborhood is defined.


00:19:22.163 --> 00:19:24.063
Mm-hmm.


00:19:24.165 --> 00:19:26.360
Can I sound like anymore
of a loser?


00:19:26.467 --> 00:19:28.560
So, um, what are you guys up to?


00:19:28.669 --> 00:19:31.331
Well, my sister's got
a birthday party in the park.


00:19:31.439 --> 00:19:33.464
I'm just bringing my book.


00:19:33.574 --> 00:19:34.734
Want to come?


00:19:34.842 --> 00:19:36.935
Uh, come?


00:19:39.514 --> 00:19:40.811
Uh, sure.


00:19:40.915 --> 00:19:43.008
( kids laughing,
talking happily )


00:19:44.752 --> 00:19:46.720
MAN:
Yeah, run.


00:19:48.423 --> 00:19:50.152
Sorry you came?


00:19:50.258 --> 00:19:52.283
Not yet.


00:19:52.393 --> 00:19:53.951
Bubbles.


00:19:54.062 --> 00:19:55.461
Bubbles, yeah.


00:19:55.563 --> 00:19:57.497
Look...
Look, there's my point.


00:19:57.598 --> 00:19:59.589
Those two kids are
the same age- she's...


00:19:59.700 --> 00:20:02.498
like, talking, using her hands,
telling stories...


00:20:02.603 --> 00:20:04.537
and he's drooling
over a cupcake.


00:20:04.639 --> 00:20:06.573
They're not the same age.


00:20:06.674 --> 00:20:07.902
How much you
want to bet?


00:20:08.009 --> 00:20:10.307
A buck says he's six months
younger than her.


00:20:10.411 --> 00:20:11.605
Buy me an ice cream?


00:20:11.712 --> 00:20:13.270
No, you're buying me one.


00:20:13.381 --> 00:20:14.541
Excuse me?


00:20:14.649 --> 00:20:15.741
Uh-huh.


00:20:15.850 --> 00:20:17.112
Is that your son?


00:20:17.218 --> 00:20:18.150
Yeah.


00:20:18.252 --> 00:20:19.549
How old is he?


00:20:19.654 --> 00:20:22.179
He's two and a half.


00:20:22.290 --> 00:20:23.314
And that little girl...


00:20:23.424 --> 00:20:24.857
do you know
how old she is?


00:20:24.959 --> 00:20:26.654
She's three months
younger.


00:20:30.064 --> 00:20:31.827
That proves nothing.


00:20:31.933 --> 00:20:34.197
Man, look at her.


00:20:34.302 --> 00:20:36.736
Have you ever seen anyone
more beautiful?


00:20:36.871 --> 00:20:37.997
So smart, too.


00:20:38.106 --> 00:20:40.267
She's just my type.


00:20:40.374 --> 00:20:41.398
Wow.


00:20:41.509 --> 00:20:44.569
I didn't even know
I had a type.


00:20:44.679 --> 00:20:46.670
Now if I could only shake
the nanny...


00:20:46.781 --> 00:20:48.408
we'd be in business.


00:20:48.516 --> 00:20:51.713
So, um, should we get
that ice cream now?


00:20:51.819 --> 00:20:52.945
Now?


00:20:53.054 --> 00:20:55.454
Well I mean, sure,
if-if you want one.


00:20:55.556 --> 00:20:58.423
Birdie, can we go get
an ice cream?


00:20:58.526 --> 00:21:00.016
Yep. Hurry back now.


00:21:00.128 --> 00:21:01.789
Uh, no, thanks.


00:21:01.896 --> 00:21:05.161
Unfortunately,
this one's on me.


00:21:05.266 --> 00:21:08.030
( chuckles )


00:21:08.136 --> 00:21:09.433
My fiirst date.


00:21:09.537 --> 00:21:10.765
The big spender.


00:21:10.872 --> 00:21:12.897
Haagen-Dazs all the way, baby.


00:21:13.007 --> 00:21:17.501
So, how come I have nothing
to say to her?


00:21:17.612 --> 00:21:20.513
Why isn't she looking at me?


00:21:20.615 --> 00:21:22.480
Am I that hideous?


00:21:22.583 --> 00:21:24.346
Do I smell?


00:21:24.452 --> 00:21:26.249
You, um, come here often?


00:21:26.354 --> 00:21:28.584
Central Park?


00:21:28.689 --> 00:21:29.986
Um, yeah.


00:21:30.091 --> 00:21:32.184
What kind of question is that?


00:21:32.293 --> 00:21:33.453
I hate myself.


00:21:33.561 --> 00:21:35.426
I live across the street,
you know.


00:21:35.530 --> 00:21:36.724
You?


00:21:36.831 --> 00:21:37.820
Me?


00:21:37.932 --> 00:21:39.263
Are you more Riverside?


00:21:39.367 --> 00:21:41.358
Yeah, I'm more
of a Riverside guy.


00:21:41.469 --> 00:21:44.529
That's really the
park, but Central
Park's pretty cool.


00:21:44.639 --> 00:21:46.197
I've done my time here.


00:21:46.307 --> 00:21:47.205
Hey, Strawberry Fields.


00:21:47.308 --> 00:21:48.798
Do you know what
it's named for?


00:21:48.910 --> 00:21:50.810
Some Beatles song, right?


00:21:50.912 --> 00:21:53.244
Close. It's actually
the name of the orphanage


00:21:53.347 --> 00:21:54.473
in Liverpool where
John Lennon


00:21:54.582 --> 00:21:56.447
used to play with his
friends who lived there.


00:21:56.551 --> 00:21:58.018
- Really?
- Yeah.


00:21:58.119 --> 00:21:59.780
I didn't know that. Neat.


00:21:59.887 --> 00:22:01.650
I took Rosemary on a tour
of the park


00:22:01.756 --> 00:22:03.690
that would make your head spin.


00:22:03.791 --> 00:22:06.225
This is my Central Park,
my New York.


00:22:06.327 --> 00:22:07.419
Yeah, they used
to have herds


00:22:07.528 --> 00:22:08.654
and hundreds
and hundreds


00:22:08.763 --> 00:22:10.731
of sheep grazing
in these fields.


00:22:10.831 --> 00:22:12.822
And then they gave
the sheepherder a job


00:22:12.934 --> 00:22:14.834
in the zoo at
the Lion House.


00:22:14.936 --> 00:22:18.099
oh, yeah, didn't the sheepherder
used to live, up in the top...


00:22:18.206 --> 00:22:24.236
( pop )


00:22:32.520 --> 00:22:33.817
( continues )


00:22:33.921 --> 00:22:34.979
See those
buildings up there?


00:22:35.089 --> 00:22:36.852
When I was younger,
I used to pretend


00:22:36.958 --> 00:22:38.755
they were pirate ships,
and I'd fight 'em.


00:22:38.859 --> 00:22:40.884
I never took you
for a pirate guy.


00:22:40.995 --> 00:22:43.054
Well, I outgrew
that eventually.


00:22:43.164 --> 00:22:44.426
( continues )


00:23:03.818 --> 00:23:08.278
( continues )


00:23:16.664 --> 00:23:19.394
( song ends )


00:23:19.500 --> 00:23:21.400
That's where my aunt's
getting married next week.


00:23:21.502 --> 00:23:24.300
GABE:
oh, the boathouse, of course.


00:23:24.405 --> 00:23:26.202
Flower girl.


00:23:26.307 --> 00:23:29.071
Ah, I'm so looking
forward to that.


00:23:29.176 --> 00:23:32.634
My aunt asked me to be
her flower girl when I was four...


00:23:32.747 --> 00:23:34.647
but, little did any
of us know...


00:23:34.749 --> 00:23:37.513
it'd take seven years for her
boyfriend to pop the question.


00:23:37.618 --> 00:23:39.051
That's hilarious.


00:23:39.153 --> 00:23:41.485
I was charming and suave.


00:23:41.589 --> 00:23:43.819
Everything you could hope to be
on your fiirst real date.


00:23:43.924 --> 00:23:45.357
Maybe we should practice
more karate.


00:23:45.459 --> 00:23:46.653
You need it.


00:23:46.761 --> 00:23:48.695
I am this close
to becoming a yellow belt.


00:23:48.796 --> 00:23:50.457
Try this close.


00:23:50.564 --> 00:23:52.122
What's tomorrow
like for you?


00:23:52.233 --> 00:23:54.201
Saturday, um...


00:23:54.302 --> 00:23:56.065
I've got cello
in the morning.


00:23:56.170 --> 00:23:58.604
And in the afternoon
I've got tap.


00:23:58.706 --> 00:24:00.071
Tap. What time
does tap end?


00:24:00.174 --> 00:24:01.402
I'm sorry.


00:24:01.509 --> 00:24:04.000
After tap, I've got this
Indian Princess thing


00:24:04.111 --> 00:24:05.305
I do with my father.


00:24:05.413 --> 00:24:07.779
Geez, it was easier
scheduling Arab-Israeli


00:24:07.882 --> 00:24:09.713
peace talks that making
a date with this girl.


00:24:09.817 --> 00:24:11.011
What's Indian Princess?


00:24:11.118 --> 00:24:12.676
It's this
""Daddy and Me'' thing.


00:24:12.787 --> 00:24:14.254
Don't ask.


00:24:14.355 --> 00:24:17.654
I just do it so he won't feel
guilty working late all week.


00:24:17.758 --> 00:24:18.747
How about Sunday?


00:24:18.859 --> 00:24:19.883
Sunday's good.


00:24:19.994 --> 00:24:21.086
Morning?


00:24:21.195 --> 00:24:22.526
In the morning
I have a tutor.


00:24:22.630 --> 00:24:24.222
But how about the afternoon?


00:24:24.332 --> 00:24:26.357
Tutor? What kind
of tutor?


00:24:26.467 --> 00:24:28.935
It's for the ERBs.


00:24:29.036 --> 00:24:32.369
My parents want me to go
