Should we call?


00:36:15.275 --> 00:36:16.333
Call?


00:36:18.011 --> 00:36:19.911
MAN ( over phone ):
Hello? Can I help you?


00:36:20.013 --> 00:36:23.073
Yes. Isaac?
We wanted to, um...


00:36:23.183 --> 00:36:25.708
arrange to see
the romantic treetop view.


00:36:25.819 --> 00:36:27.309
( man speaking over phone,
indistinctly )


00:36:27.421 --> 00:36:29.480
Something right in the range
of your place.


00:36:29.589 --> 00:36:30.578
Yes.


00:36:30.690 --> 00:36:32.089
Maybe it is true.


00:36:32.192 --> 00:36:34.786
Maybe girls do mature
faster than boys.


00:36:34.895 --> 00:36:36.328
Could I talk like that?


00:36:36.430 --> 00:36:38.489
How is tomorrow afternoon
for you?


00:36:38.598 --> 00:36:42.591
Tomorrow for me?
It's, uh...


00:36:42.702 --> 00:36:44.329
It's good.


00:36:44.438 --> 00:36:46.702
Yes, that'd be perfect.


00:36:46.807 --> 00:36:50.004
3:00? See you there.


00:36:50.110 --> 00:36:51.771
3:00 tomorrow.


00:36:51.878 --> 00:36:53.277
Right.


00:36:53.380 --> 00:36:55.871
( door opens, closes )


00:36:55.982 --> 00:36:56.949
QUick.


00:36:58.552 --> 00:37:01.180
Here. Hurry. Hurry.


00:37:02.222 --> 00:37:03.655
ADAM:
Are you back here?


00:37:03.757 --> 00:37:05.156
Got some new kicking tees.


00:37:05.258 --> 00:37:07.192
They're titanium.


00:37:07.294 --> 00:37:08.261
oh.


00:37:09.763 --> 00:37:11.025
How's it going?


00:37:11.131 --> 00:37:12.894
Good.


00:37:12.999 --> 00:37:15.433
Dad, you remember
Rosemary Telesco, right?


00:37:18.472 --> 00:37:21.669
From kindergarten. Sure.


00:37:21.775 --> 00:37:22.639
Hey.


00:37:22.742 --> 00:37:26.303
Hi. Long time, no see.


00:37:27.647 --> 00:37:29.877
She's in my
karate class, Dad.


00:37:29.983 --> 00:37:31.712
Cool.


00:37:34.888 --> 00:37:37.516
But she wasn'tjust
in my karate class anymore.


00:37:37.624 --> 00:37:40.855
oh, no.
She was in my life.


00:37:40.961 --> 00:37:42.588
We were going out
to look for an apartment


00:37:42.696 --> 00:37:44.095
for my father tomorrow.


00:37:44.197 --> 00:37:47.394
These are things boyfriends
and girlfriends do.


00:37:47.501 --> 00:37:50.629
What other things do boyfriends
and girlfriends do?


00:37:53.707 --> 00:37:56.039
Someone
need a ride?


00:37:56.143 --> 00:37:59.670
So, I'll see you tomorrow: 2:30.


00:37:59.779 --> 00:38:01.713
Yeah. See you tomorrow.


00:38:05.418 --> 00:38:07.511
Are there any
more beautiful words


00:38:07.621 --> 00:38:11.057
in the English dictionary
than ""See you tomorrow'?


00:38:11.158 --> 00:38:13.149
oh, the plan was perfect.


00:38:13.260 --> 00:38:14.784
She would tell
her friend, Libby...


00:38:14.895 --> 00:38:16.726
to say Rosemary's playing
over at her house.


00:38:16.830 --> 00:38:18.559
...from, like, 2:30
until around dinnertime.


00:38:18.665 --> 00:38:21.463
See, Libby had a grandmother
who took care ofher...


00:38:21.568 --> 00:38:22.830
and was literally deaf.


00:38:22.936 --> 00:38:25.029
Would never hear the phone
if it rang.


00:38:25.138 --> 00:38:26.435
So her story was solid.


00:38:26.540 --> 00:38:28.405
( on TV):
Let's try ""Anagrammed Birds'' for $200.


00:38:28.508 --> 00:38:31.705
I would tell my friend
Max Kavinsky to cover for me.


00:38:31.811 --> 00:38:33.779
The only possible flaw
in my plan


00:38:33.880 --> 00:38:36.246
was that I didn't
actually have the guts


00:38:36.349 --> 00:38:39.147
to tell Max that
I was hanging out with a girl.


00:38:39.252 --> 00:38:42.744
So,you know, I, like, never
actually had the conversation.


00:38:42.856 --> 00:38:44.585
Luckily, I knew Max was going


00:38:44.691 --> 00:38:46.591
to Six Flags
for the entire day...


00:38:46.693 --> 00:38:48.092
I got this.


00:38:48.195 --> 00:38:49.856
...so I knew he wasn't
going to accidentally call...


00:38:49.963 --> 00:38:53.524
looking for me,
or anYThing.


00:38:58.305 --> 00:39:00.933
You, um... ride
the subway a lot


00:39:01.041 --> 00:39:02.565
without any grown-ups?


00:39:02.676 --> 00:39:06.373
Actually, no. I...


00:39:06.479 --> 00:39:08.174
I do it all
the time, you know.


00:39:08.281 --> 00:39:09.805
It's much more
fun this way.


00:39:09.916 --> 00:39:11.850
I didn't have the heart
to tell her


00:39:11.952 --> 00:39:13.886
I'd never been
south of West 7 2nd.


00:39:13.987 --> 00:39:15.852
I felt she needed
my leadership.


00:39:19.926 --> 00:39:21.985
Greenwich Village
might as well have been


00:39:22.095 --> 00:39:23.289
a thousand miles away.


00:39:23.396 --> 00:39:28.766
I think we might have gotten off
a stop or two early.


00:39:30.003 --> 00:39:32.403
Do you, um...


00:39:32.505 --> 00:39:34.063
Do you want a ride?


00:39:34.174 --> 00:39:35.573
You think
we can both fit?


00:39:35.675 --> 00:39:37.734
We can try.


00:39:37.844 --> 00:39:39.971
Come on. Get on.


00:39:53.026 --> 00:39:55.620
With that girl's
arms around me...


00:39:55.729 --> 00:39:57.959
there was nothing
I couldn't do.


00:39:58.064 --> 00:39:59.827
I think it's this way.


00:39:59.933 --> 00:40:03.096
With the possible
exception of,uh...


00:40:03.203 --> 00:40:05.194
fiinding that apartment
we were looking for.


00:40:13.246 --> 00:40:15.646
Deja vu.


00:40:15.749 --> 00:40:19.685
Uh, maybe we should
ask for directions.


00:40:19.786 --> 00:40:23.187
No. I think it's just right
up this alley right here.


00:40:23.290 --> 00:40:26.726
You are so like all
the guys in my family.


00:40:35.335 --> 00:40:38.065
- That your girlfriend?
- Excuse me?


00:40:38.171 --> 00:40:39.536
She your girl?


00:40:39.639 --> 00:40:42.199
Yeah. My girlfriend.


00:40:42.309 --> 00:40:44.470
Huh.


00:40:44.577 --> 00:40:47.808
I had a girlfriend
once upon a time, too.


00:40:47.914 --> 00:40:49.814
She trampled
my heart.


00:40:49.916 --> 00:40:51.577
Left me bleeding on the floor.


00:40:51.685 --> 00:40:53.016
Run.


00:40:53.119 --> 00:40:54.347
What?


00:40:54.454 --> 00:40:57.252
Run while you
still can, brother.


00:40:57.357 --> 00:40:59.917
Take my advice.


00:41:00.026 --> 00:41:01.721
Make like the wind.


00:41:02.862 --> 00:41:04.193
We were close.


00:41:04.297 --> 00:41:06.925
one block, a left,
and then another left.


00:41:07.033 --> 00:41:08.500
Let's go.


00:41:20.847 --> 00:41:22.314
Are you Isaac?


00:41:22.415 --> 00:41:25.179
I'm Rosemary.


00:41:25.285 --> 00:41:27.253
We're here to
see the apartment.


00:41:27.354 --> 00:41:29.652
Am I getting Punk'd?


00:41:29.756 --> 00:41:31.155
No. It's for my dad.


00:41:31.257 --> 00:41:33.191
And will Daddy
be meeting us here?


00:41:33.293 --> 00:41:35.124
Well, he will if I give him
the high sign.


00:41:35.228 --> 00:41:36.820
Trying to make a
commission or not?


00:41:39.099 --> 00:41:41.090
ISAAC:
We do a nice


00:41:41.201 --> 00:41:43.829
business in two bedrooms
with divorced fathers.


00:41:43.937 --> 00:41:45.234
This place
will be gone


00:41:45.338 --> 00:41:48.569
in a New York minute,
I promise you.


00:41:48.675 --> 00:41:50.836
Wood-burning fireplace.


00:41:52.312 --> 00:41:54.974
oh, yeah, I noticed.


00:41:55.081 --> 00:41:57.208
I didn't know what
we were looking for exactly.


00:41:57.317 --> 00:42:00.309
What do you think?


00:42:00.420 --> 00:42:02.581
I like it.


00:42:02.689 --> 00:42:04.486
It's nice. Amazing.


00:42:04.591 --> 00:42:06.354
But I knew one thing
for certain..


00:42:06.459 --> 00:42:08.324
Yeah.


00:42:08.428 --> 00:42:11.158
It was the most romantic
treetop view I ever saw.


00:42:14.534 --> 00:42:14.768
We came home up the bike path
along the Hudson.


00:42:14.768 --> 00:42:17.931
We came home up the bike path
along the Hudson.


00:42:18.037 --> 00:42:20.198
67 blocks.


00:42:20.306 --> 00:42:21.967
The most physically
grueling experience


00:42:22.075 --> 00:42:24.635
of my short life
on this planet.


00:42:24.744 --> 00:42:26.644
But I barely felt it.


00:42:26.746 --> 00:42:30.045
I never felt
so ridiculously wonderful.


00:42:32.085 --> 00:42:35.612
This was New York the way
I always want to remember it.


00:42:35.722 --> 00:42:37.622
Aplace where
anYThing is possible.


00:42:37.724 --> 00:42:39.658
The city of dreams.


00:42:39.759 --> 00:42:41.693
( alternative )


00:43:09.789 --> 00:43:13.418
( song ends )


00:43:13.526 --> 00:43:14.754
What's this?


00:43:14.861 --> 00:43:16.260
oh, this?


00:43:16.362 --> 00:43:17.852
You don't
know about this?


00:43:17.964 --> 00:43:20.398
It's the smallest park
in New York City.


00:43:20.500 --> 00:43:23.697
Some commissioner died and
left his whole townhouse


00:43:23.803 --> 00:43:26.533
to be knocked
down for a park.


00:43:26.639 --> 00:43:28.937
How come
I didn't know about this?


00:43:29.042 --> 00:43:30.441
Nobody on your
side of Broadway


00:43:30.543 --> 00:43:31.942
ever comes
over this way.


00:43:32.045 --> 00:43:34.013
That's what's so cool
about West End.


00:43:46.159 --> 00:43:47.854
Do you come
here a lot?


00:43:47.961 --> 00:43:49.360
Actually, I, um...


00:43:49.462 --> 00:43:52.795
I haven't been here
in quite a while.


00:44:00.440 --> 00:44:03.034
Hey! Mini-Me!


00:44:04.444 --> 00:44:06.002
What are you doing in my park?


00:44:06.112 --> 00:44:07.170
oh, no way.


00:44:07.280 --> 00:44:09.043
Not Darryl Kitzens.
Not now.


00:44:09.148 --> 00:44:10.172
It's a public park.


00:44:10.283 --> 00:44:13.480
What's she doing,
inciting him?


00:44:13.586 --> 00:44:16.487
Doesn't she know that wild
animals need to be placated?


00:44:16.589 --> 00:44:18.614
I... I think this
park's big enough


00:44:18.725 --> 00:44:20.488
for all of us, right?


00:44:20.593 --> 00:44:21.958
Who were we kidding?


00:44:22.061 --> 00:44:25.189
A white belt and a yellow belt
facing off


00:44:25.298 --> 00:44:26.925
against the Darth Maul
of PS 87?


00:44:27.033 --> 00:44:29.695
We were gonna get creamed.


00:44:35.808 --> 00:44:38.177
You picked the wrong park,
little man.


00:44:38.177 --> 00:44:38.700
You picked the wrong park,
little man.


00:44:38.811 --> 00:44:40.642
( growls ):
Get the hell
out of my park!


00:44:40.747 --> 00:44:42.112
- Ki-yah!
- ( screams )


00:44:42.215 --> 00:44:43.079
You're dead!


00:44:45.084 --> 00:44:46.051
Ki-yah!


00:44:47.754 --> 00:44:49.016
Ki-yah!


00:44:54.594 --> 00:44:55.788
( groans )


00:44:55.895 --> 00:44:57.362
Come on!
Run, run! Hurry!


00:45:00.900 --> 00:45:02.561
Hop on.


00:45:02.669 --> 00:45:04.261
Go, go, go, go,
go, go, go!


00:45:06.506 --> 00:45:08.701
RoSEMARY:
He's coming! He's coming!


00:45:11.077 --> 00:45:13.102
Go faster! Go! Go!


00:45:16.182 --> 00:45:19.276
RoSEMARY:
Make the light! Go on!


00:45:20.853 --> 00:45:24.789
( car tires screeching,
horns honking )


00:45:36.703 --> 00:45:40.434
We were both still flushed
from our day of adventure.


00:45:40.540 --> 00:45:42.235
Well, good night.


00:45:42.342 --> 00:45:43.400
Good night.


00:45:43.509 --> 00:45:45.943
I could do battle
with Darryl Kitzens.


00:45:46.045 --> 00:45:48.570
So why can't
I just lean in to her?


00:45:48.681 --> 00:45:51.081
Do it.
Do it,you wimp, do it.


00:45:53.219 --> 00:45:54.709
That was fun.


00:45:54.821 --> 00:45:56.721
Yeah, it was.


00:45:56.823 --> 00:45:58.916
Scared he's going
to hunt us down?


00:45:59.025 --> 00:46:01.118
I just have to
keep a low profile


00:46:01.227 --> 00:46:02.558
for the rest of the summer.


00:46:02.662 --> 00:46:05.460
And, of course, transfer to
a military school in the fall.


00:46:05.565 --> 00:46:10.730
I just have to keep a low
profile for one more week.


00:46:10.837 --> 00:46:12.566
A week?


00:46:12.672 --> 00:46:14.572
Well, next Sunday,
after the wedding...


00:46:14.674 --> 00:46:15.766
I'm going to camp.


00:46:15.875 --> 00:46:17.433
Camp?


00:46:17.543 --> 00:46:19.636
For how long?


00:46:19.746 --> 00:46:21.077
For six weeks.


00:46:21.180 --> 00:46:23.080
Six weeks?


00:46:23.182 --> 00:46:25.480
She might as well
have said she's dying.


00:46:25.585 --> 00:46:27.746
That's fantastic.


00:46:27.854 --> 00:46:30.345
Yeah.


00:46:44.437 --> 00:46:49.272
Well... I better
get inside.


00:46:49.375 --> 00:46:51.104
Yeah.


00:46:51.210 --> 00:46:52.609
Good night.


00:46:52.712 --> 00:46:54.270
Good night.


00:47:03.723 --> 00:47:05.350
DooRMAN:
Miss.


00:47:15.034 --> 00:47:17.559
What if she goes to camp
and I never get to kiss her?


00:47:17.670 --> 00:47:19.228
That's the way
it's going to be.


00:47:19.338 --> 00:47:20.737
It's so obvious.


00:47:20.840 --> 00:47:23.331
Every opportunity I have
will go the same way.


00:47:23.443 --> 00:47:25.274
""Good night. '
""Good night. 'No.


00:47:25.378 --> 00:47:26.936
I will not let that happen.


00:47:27.046 --> 00:47:29.537
I will kiss her before
she gets on that bus to Maine.


00:47:29.649 --> 00:47:31.378
I will, I will, I will.!


00:47:42.161 --> 00:47:45.187
Gabe?! Ga...!
That's him!


00:47:45.298 --> 00:47:46.765
There he is.
oh, thank God.


00:47:46.866 --> 00:47:48.993
If they don't kill you,
I'm going to.


00:47:49.102 --> 00:47:51.400
So it, um, it turns out
Max Kavinsky didn't go


00:47:51.504 --> 00:47:52.698
to Six Flags after all.


00:47:52.805 --> 00:47:54.204
He got sick.


00:47:54.307 --> 00:47:55.740
My mother actually ended up


00:47:55.842 --> 00:47:57.969
running into his mother
at the Fairway...


00:47:58.077 --> 00:47:59.772
and, well, they got to talking.


00:47:59.879 --> 00:48:01.972
What?


00:48:02.081 --> 00:48:04.379
Gabe, come here!


00:48:04.484 --> 00:48:05.542
Come here.


00:48:06.652 --> 00:48:08.779
Don't you ever
go anywhere again


00:48:08.888 --> 00:48:10.788
without us knowing
where you are...


00:48:10.890 --> 00:48:11.982
do you hear me?


00:48:12.091 --> 00:48:14.082
( crying ):
You had us scared half to death.


00:48:14.193 --> 00:48:15.353
GABE:
My punishment..


00:48:15.461 --> 00:48:17.793
no phone, no TV...


00:48:17.897 --> 00:48:19.364
no leaving the apartment
for 48 hours.


00:48:19.465 --> 00:48:21.990
It was the fiirst thing
my parents agreed on


00:48:22.101 --> 00:48:23.193
in a very long time.


00:48:23.302 --> 00:48:24.462
LESLI E:
Do I have to call Rosemary's mother?


00:48:24.570 --> 00:48:26.037
- Is that what I have to do?
- No! No!


00:48:26.139 --> 00:48:28.937
- Don't call anyone.
- I thought, I thought
we had an understanding


00:48:29.041 --> 00:48:30.508
- on the nine square blocks-
- We do!


00:48:30.610 --> 00:48:32.475
that the only way that this
can work, your dad and I...


00:48:32.578 --> 00:48:34.512
I had to throw myself
on the mercy of the court


00:48:34.614 --> 00:48:36.809
just to get special permission
to go to karate class.


00:48:36.916 --> 00:48:38.178
I'll do anything!


00:48:38.284 --> 00:48:39.945
I'll wash dishes for
the rest of the summer!


00:48:40.052 --> 00:48:41.314
I promise I will!


00:48:41.420 --> 00:48:44.912
Itjust wasn't an option
to miss that class.


00:48:45.024 --> 00:48:47.390
ADAM:
You scared the hell
out of us today.


00:48:49.262 --> 00:48:50.490
I know, I'm sorry.


00:48:50.596 --> 00:48:51.585
Yeah, what
does sorry mean?


00:48:51.697 --> 00:48:53.392
Sorry means I'm not
gonna do it again.


00:48:53.499 --> 00:48:54.966
- That's right. Never again.
- Right.


00:48:55.067 --> 00:48:56.227
- Right?
- Right.


00:48:57.336 --> 00:48:59.361
Hey, Dad?


00:48:59.472 --> 00:49:00.700
Yeah.


00:49:00.807 --> 00:49:04.299
Are... Are you gonna move out?


00:49:08.214 --> 00:49:10.978
Eventually, yeah, I am, Gabe.


00:49:11.083 --> 00:49:13.916
Well, I, um...


00:49:14.020 --> 00:49:15.715
I found an apartment for you.


00:49:15.822 --> 00:49:17.050
You what?


00:49:17.156 --> 00:49:18.555
That's where I went today.


00:49:18.658 --> 00:49:21.923
To look for an
apartment for you.


00:49:22.028 --> 00:49:23.461
Do you want me to move out?


00:49:23.563 --> 00:49:26.123
No, no, of course not,
but, you know...


00:49:26.232 --> 00:49:31.329
maybe we can't get our lives
started again until you do.


00:49:32.738 --> 00:49:35.400
Where do you get such big ideas?


00:49:35.508 --> 00:49:38.500
I don't know. I just get them.


00:49:38.611 --> 00:49:40.135
So w-where is
this apartment?


00:49:40.246 --> 00:49:42.373
It's a two-bedroom
on Grove Street.


00:49:42.481 --> 00:49:43.971
In the Village?


00:49:44.083 --> 00:49:45.414
Yeah, wood-burning fireplace.


00:49:45.518 --> 00:49:46.416
No way.


00:49:46.519 --> 00:49:47.417
Why not?


00:49:47.520 --> 00:49:50.114
It's too far
from you, champ.


00:49:50.223 --> 00:49:53.351
I-I wouldn't move
more than...


00:49:53.459 --> 00:49:56.758
a three- or four-block
radius from you.


00:49:56.863 --> 00:49:59.889
You'd have to go to college
to get farther away from me.


00:50:01.033 --> 00:50:02.022
okay?


00:50:02.134 --> 00:50:03.328
okay.


00:50:03.436 --> 00:50:04.562
Go to sleep.


00:50:04.670 --> 00:50:05.637
All right.


00:50:07.340 --> 00:50:10.537
So, uh, what's the deal
with this Rosemary?


00:50:10.643 --> 00:50:12.474
Rosemary?


00:50:12.578 --> 00:50:14.443
How do you mean?


00:50:14.547 --> 00:50:16.913
Nothing.


00:50:17.016 --> 00:50:20.577
I-I, I'm just not used to...


00:50:20.686 --> 00:50:22.813
We do karate
together, Dad.


00:50:22.922 --> 00:50:24.685
Sh-she's my sparring partner.


00:50:24.790 --> 00:50:27.350
oh.


00:50:27.460 --> 00:50:29.928
okay, great.


00:50:30.029 --> 00:50:31.053
I didn't even pick her.


00:50:31.163 --> 00:50:33.154
Whatever you say, king.


00:50:37.370 --> 00:50:39.930
That night, I had this dream.


00:50:48.681 --> 00:50:49.648
All right! Yeah!


00:50:54.353 --> 00:50:55.251
RoSEMARY:
Gabe...


00:50:55.354 --> 00:50:56.286
Gabe!


00:50:56.389 --> 00:50:58.380
BoY:
I'm open! Gabe!


00:50:58.491 --> 00:51:01.483
( whispering ):
over here...


00:51:01.594 --> 00:51:03.186
BoY:
over to Eric!


00:51:03.296 --> 00:51:04.490
Go, man! Run!


00:51:04.597 --> 00:51:05.894
BoY 2:
Hey!


00:51:05.998 --> 00:51:07.898
RoSEMARY:
Gabe... Gabe...


00:51:08.000 --> 00:51:09.695
( cloth ripping )


00:51:14.407 --> 00:51:15.305
Where are you going?


00:51:15.408 --> 00:51:17.433
You're ditching us for her?


00:51:17.543 --> 00:51:18.567
oh, come on.


00:51:22.848 --> 00:51:24.577
Aw, dude.


00:51:24.684 --> 00:51:25.651
Disgusting.


00:51:32.091 --> 00:51:35.652
The next day, I couldn't
get to class fast enough.


00:51:35.761 --> 00:51:37.422
I was gonna
be near her again...


00:51:37.530 --> 00:51:38.861
grapple with her...


00:51:38.965 --> 00:51:40.296
smell her hair.


00:51:40.399 --> 00:51:41.593
Ki-yah!


00:51:41.701 --> 00:51:43.931
That day
the Gates of Hell opened...


00:51:44.036 --> 00:51:45.799
and Tim Staples
walked right through.


00:51:45.905 --> 00:51:47.964
TEACHER:
So, we're gonna shift sparring partners


00:51:48.074 --> 00:51:50.474
to make sure everyone's
with their level.


00:51:50.576 --> 00:51:53.943
That means Tim-
you'll be with Rosemary.


00:51:54.046 --> 00:51:55.274
Could this be?


00:51:55.381 --> 00:51:57.906
My woman getting ripped
from my hands like this?


00:51:58.017 --> 00:51:59.951
I could see where
all this leads.


00:52:00.052 --> 00:52:02.043
Do you, Rosemary Telesco...


00:52:02.154 --> 00:52:04.748
take Tim Staples to be
your lawfully wedded husband?


00:52:04.857 --> 00:52:05.789
( banging )


00:52:05.891 --> 00:52:07.950
No...!


00:52:08.060 --> 00:52:09.152
Rosemary!


00:52:09.261 --> 00:52:12.162
And Gabe, your new
sparring partner


00:52:12.264 --> 00:52:15.290
will be David Betanahu.


00:52:15.401 --> 00:52:16.425
This is my level?


00:52:16.535 --> 00:52:18.730
David Betanahu?


00:52:18.838 --> 00:52:20.305
How could this happen?


00:52:20.406 --> 00:52:21.998
She's with Ashton Kutcher
over there...


00:52:22.108 --> 00:52:25.043
and I'm with the sweatiest
ten-year-old in Manhattan.


00:52:25.144 --> 00:52:26.634
The kid's practically
had a moustache


00:52:26.746 --> 00:52:28.111
since he was in nursery school.


00:52:33.753 --> 00:52:37.382
Everything I took for granted-
stolen in a New York minute.


00:52:37.490 --> 00:52:38.252
DAVI D:
Ki-yah!


00:52:38.357 --> 00:52:39.255
Somehow...


00:52:39.358 --> 00:52:40.689
Ki-yah!


00:52:40.793 --> 00:52:43.091
...karate wasn't quite the same
without Rosemary.


00:52:45.031 --> 00:52:47.795
So... how was
that class for you?


00:52:47.900 --> 00:52:49.231
Was it a good one?


00:52:49.335 --> 00:52:51.599
Um, I'm having a little trouble


00:52:51.704 --> 00:52:53.262
with this Mochizuki maneuver.


00:52:53.372 --> 00:52:55.067
Yeah, yeah,
me, me too.


00:52:55.174 --> 00:52:56.072
I couldn't resist.


00:52:56.175 --> 00:52:57.608
I needed more and more pain.


00:52:57.710 --> 00:53:00.941
So, uh, how's, how's
that Tim guy at the Mochizuki?


00:53:01.047 --> 00:53:03.277
He's a lot
better than me...


00:53:03.382 --> 00:53:05.873
but he wants us to
practice together.


00:53:05.985 --> 00:53:07.816
oh, r-r-really?


00:53:07.920 --> 00:53:09.945
Wow, th-that's terrific.


00:53:10.056 --> 00:53:12.752
You know, hey, when,
when can we get together?


00:53:12.858 --> 00:53:17.295
Well, I've got cello this
afternoon, so, not today.


00:53:17.396 --> 00:53:18.363
Cello?


00:53:18.464 --> 00:53:19.954
But I thought cello
was on Saturdays.


00:53:20.066 --> 00:53:21.624
Tuesday and
Saturday.


00:53:21.734 --> 00:53:23.702
She can't cancel
her frickin'cello lesson?


00:53:23.803 --> 00:53:25.168
Doesn't she know
our days are numbered


00:53:25.271 --> 00:53:26.295
before that bus to camp?


00:53:26.405 --> 00:53:28.305
How 'bout I call you?


00:53:28.407 --> 00:53:30.637
Sure.
Sounds great.


00:53:30.743 --> 00:53:32.836
So that's it?


00:53:32.945 --> 00:53:35.914
just a lousy ""call you'?


00:53:36.015 --> 00:53:37.380
Not even an ""I'll call you. '


00:53:37.483 --> 00:53:39.542
A ""how 'bout I call you'?


00:53:39.652 --> 00:53:41.916
What on earth does that mean?


00:53:42.021 --> 00:53:43.545
When?.!


00:53:43.656 --> 00:53:44.850
( beep )


00:53:44.957 --> 00:53:47.517
You have no new messages.


00:53:50.362 --> 00:53:52.262
What choice did I have,
but to return


00:53:52.364 --> 00:53:54.127
to my old, miserable life?


00:53:54.233 --> 00:53:55.257
Wait a minute.


00:53:55.367 --> 00:53:57.267
You were happy.


00:53:57.369 --> 00:53:58.961
oh, please.!
I was miserable.


00:53:59.071 --> 00:54:00.402
I just didn't know


00:54:00.506 --> 00:54:02.838
how miserable I was.


00:54:02.942 --> 00:54:03.840
Whoa.


00:54:03.943 --> 00:54:04.841
ADAM:
Heads up!


00:54:04.944 --> 00:54:06.138
( shrieks )
Whoa.


00:54:06.245 --> 00:54:07.712
- MAN: Watch it!
- Sorry.


00:54:09.515 --> 00:54:12.609
Where's your head
today, G-man?


00:54:12.718 --> 00:54:14.015
My head?


00:54:14.120 --> 00:54:15.485
Yeah, it's not with the ball.


00:54:15.588 --> 00:54:16.520
What was that?


00:54:16.622 --> 00:54:18.852
It's, it's not my head, Dad.


00:54:18.958 --> 00:54:21.290
It's, um... it's my leg.


00:54:21.393 --> 00:54:22.951
I hurt it in karate class.


00:54:23.062 --> 00:54:24.825
Karate.
See, guys like us...


00:54:24.930 --> 00:54:26.488
we weren't built
for kicking bricks.


00:54:26.599 --> 00:54:28.965
Let's keep our
priorities in line.


00:54:29.068 --> 00:54:30.695
Eyes on the prize.


00:54:33.873 --> 00:54:34.840
Go. Sweet spot.


00:54:34.940 --> 00:54:36.339
- one, two, three...
- He was right.


00:54:36.442 --> 00:54:37.841
My priorities
were all screwed up.


00:54:37.943 --> 00:54:38.875
I was an athlete.


00:54:38.978 --> 00:54:40.309
I just had to shake it off.


00:54:40.412 --> 00:54:41.572
Yeah!


00:54:43.415 --> 00:54:44.473
Look at me.


00:54:44.583 --> 00:54:46.107
I can bounce back.


00:54:46.218 --> 00:54:49.210
I don't need some girl
in my life for me to be happy.


00:54:49.321 --> 00:54:52.415
( phone ringing )


00:54:57.329 --> 00:54:58.694
Hello.


00:54:58.797 --> 00:55:00.355
Yeah.


00:55:00.466 --> 00:55:01.797
You know what?
I really hate it


00:55:01.901 --> 00:55:03.163
when people
call me at home


00:55:03.269 --> 00:55:04.463
and try to sell me stuff.


00:55:06.438 --> 00:55:07.928
That's okay.


00:55:08.040 --> 00:55:09.337
okay. Bye.


00:55:15.381 --> 00:55:19.340
( phone ringing )


00:55:19.451 --> 00:55:21.942
Hello.


00:55:22.054 --> 00:55:24.284
Hi.


00:55:24.390 --> 00:55:25.550
Yeah, he's right here.


00:55:25.658 --> 00:55:26.625
Gabe.


00:55:28.494 --> 00:55:29.461
It's a girl.


00:55:37.403 --> 00:55:38.301
I got it!


00:55:38.404 --> 00:55:39.496
ADAM ( on phone ):
Got it?


00:55:39.605 --> 00:55:40.572
I got it!


00:55:43.342 --> 00:55:44.434
Hey.


00:55:44.543 --> 00:55:45.908
RoSEMARY:
I said I was gonna call.


00:55:46.011 --> 00:55:47.444
Did you?


00:55:47.546 --> 00:55:49.207
I don't even remember.


00:55:49.315 --> 00:55:51.283
Smooth under pressure.


00:55:51.383 --> 00:55:52.748
- ( heart beating )
- That's me.


00:55:52.851 --> 00:55:55.217
If only I could do something
about the beating of my heart.


00:55:55.321 --> 00:55:56.345
( heart beating )


00:55:56.455 --> 00:55:58.013
Could she hear that
through the phone?


00:55:58.123 --> 00:55:59.818
So what are you
doing tomorrow night?


00:55:59.925 --> 00:56:01.950
Um, tomorrow night?


00:56:02.061 --> 00:56:06.088
Yeah, it's summer, so it's not
like a school night or anything.


00:56:06.198 --> 00:56:07.893
Uh, I-I'm free, totally.


00:56:08.000 --> 00:56:09.831
'Cause my parents
got these special tickets


00:56:09.935 --> 00:56:12.631
to this concert with this guy
who's supposed to be, like...


00:56:12.738 --> 00:56:14.603
the greatest singer
in New York or something.


00:56:14.707 --> 00:56:17.938
Do you, um, want to go?


00:56:18.043 --> 00:56:20.807
Uh, me, me, me and your parents?


00:56:20.913 --> 00:56:22.380
And me, too.


00:56:22.481 --> 00:56:24.813
My mom said I could
invite anyone I want.


00:56:24.917 --> 00:56:26.111
Sounds awesome.


00:56:26.218 --> 00:56:27.116
Great.


00:56:27.219 --> 00:56:28.311
She called.


00:56:28.454 --> 00:56:30.581
She said she was gonna call
and she kept her word.


00:56:30.689 --> 00:56:31.815
This was notjust some fiigment


00:56:31.924 --> 00:56:33.152
of my imagination.


00:56:33.259 --> 00:56:36.194
our love is a two-way street.


00:56:40.065 --> 00:56:42.556
Hey.


00:56:42.668 --> 00:56:44.226
You're looking
sharp there, tiger.


00:56:44.336 --> 00:56:46.065
Like I even care.


00:56:46.171 --> 00:56:48.162
Nice.


00:56:48.274 --> 00:56:49.798
I especially
like the hair.


00:56:53.312 --> 00:56:54.609
Come on, mess it up.


00:56:56.749 --> 00:56:59.115
Don't take all your romantic
advice from him, Gabe.


00:56:59.218 --> 00:57:02.619
You look very nice.


00:57:02.721 --> 00:57:04.518
I, um, I'm gonna
wait downstairs.


00:57:04.623 --> 00:57:07.183
Do you want us to come down
and say hi to her parents?


00:57:07.293 --> 00:57:09.420
No.


00:57:09.528 --> 00:57:10.927
Excuse me.


00:57:11.030 --> 00:57:12.998
They said they'd have you
home by 1 1 :00...


00:57:13.098 --> 00:57:16.431
and if you're gonna be one
second later, I'll need a call.


00:57:16.535 --> 00:57:20.096
okay.


00:57:20.205 --> 00:57:22.435
our little boy
is growing up, huh?


00:57:22.541 --> 00:57:24.133
Yeah, he is.


00:57:32.117 --> 00:57:33.641
Pretty snazzy.


00:57:33.752 --> 00:57:34.946
Big night?


00:57:35.054 --> 00:57:37.386
Just some date
with some girl-


00:57:37.489 --> 00:57:40.117
you know, nothing,
nothing big.


00:57:40.225 --> 00:57:42.386
That girl that came by here
the other day?


00:57:42.494 --> 00:57:45.019
That'd be the one.


00:57:45.130 --> 00:57:48.122
She was a nice girl,
that girl that came by here.


00:57:48.233 --> 00:57:51.100
All right, Mr. Gabe.


00:57:54.173 --> 00:57:55.697
Hey, Gabe.


00:57:55.808 --> 00:57:56.797
Nice to see you.


00:57:56.909 --> 00:57:57.807
You, too.


00:57:57.910 --> 00:57:59.673
Thanks for joining us.


00:57:59.778 --> 00:58:00.676
Hi, Mrs. Telesco.


00:58:00.779 --> 00:58:02.974
MRS. TELESCo:
Hello. How are you?


00:58:03.082 --> 00:58:05.277
Good.


00:58:12.324 --> 00:58:13.848
Welcome to The Carlyle.


00:58:16.762 --> 00:58:17.729
Ma'am.


00:58:23.635 --> 00:58:27.002
Yeah, Mickey took me
here on our third date.


00:58:27.106 --> 00:58:29.074
We had to stand right
over there by the bar


00:58:29.174 --> 00:58:30.334
because we couldn't
afford a table.


00:58:30.442 --> 00:58:31.875
And from that
moment on...


00:58:31.977 --> 00:58:34.275
there was
no turning back for us.


00:58:34.380 --> 00:58:36.848
( applause )


00:58:36.949 --> 00:58:38.143
You're gonna love this guy.


00:58:38.250 --> 00:58:40.115
No one sings
like Loston Harris.


00:58:40.219 --> 00:58:41.914
This guy is New York.


00:58:42.020 --> 00:58:46.150
( slowjazz intro playing )


00:58:47.993 --> 00:58:53.021
( jazz standard )


00:58:55.267 --> 00:58:57.701
I can't tell you what
that fiirst song was about.


00:58:57.803 --> 00:59:00.772
Something about love
and a boy and a girl...


00:59:00.873 --> 00:59:02.738
and this boy
can think of nothing


00:59:02.841 --> 00:59:05.036
but holding that
girl's hand in the darkness.


00:59:05.144 --> 00:59:07.578
( continues )


00:59:13.318 --> 00:59:15.650
I'm not sure how
I got the courage.


00:59:15.754 --> 00:59:18.245
Maybe it was the buzz
from the Shirley Temple.


00:59:18.357 --> 00:59:20.416
Maybe it was Loston Harris-


00:59:20.526 --> 00:59:22.426
the greatest singer this
little town has ever known.


00:59:22.528 --> 00:59:26.897
But I knew our relationship
had to get to the next step...


00:59:26.999 --> 00:59:31.459
or Rosemary and I wouldjust
remain karate friends forever.


00:59:31.570 --> 00:59:33.333
( continues )


00:59:50.756 --> 00:59:52.519
Never had I been
so keenly aware


00:59:52.624 --> 00:59:56.958
of the ability of my palm
to manufacture sweat.


00:59:57.062 --> 00:59:59.053
But I was determined to hold
that girl's hand


00:59:59.164 --> 01:00:01.132
for every single second.


01:00:04.069 --> 01:00:06.128
What does this mean?
Does she hate me?


01:00:06.238 --> 01:00:08.035
Is she grossed out by me?


01:00:08.140 --> 01:00:10.040
Am I pushing everything
way too fast?


01:00:18.417 --> 01:00:21.284
All those ridiculous
songs about love-


01:00:21.386 --> 01:00:22.785
I fiinally understood.


01:00:22.888 --> 01:00:23.889
( song ends, applause )


01:00:23.889 --> 01:00:25.948
( song ends, applause )


01:00:26.058 --> 01:00:28.253
Forget the second stop.


01:00:28.360 --> 01:00:30.521
We're gonna walk
from here, too.


01:00:30.629 --> 01:00:31.926
Thanks.


01:00:33.599 --> 01:00:34.964
Thanks.


01:00:37.135 --> 01:00:39.899
Well, uh, you guys
say your good nights now...


01:00:40.005 --> 01:00:42.098
and, uh, Daddy and I
are gonna get some milk


01:00:42.207 --> 01:00:44.971
for breakfast tomorrow, okay?
So...


01:00:45.077 --> 01:00:47.204
Good night, Mrs. Telesco.


01:00:47.312 --> 01:00:49.212
oh, thank you
for coming, Gabe.


01:00:49.314 --> 01:00:50.576
oh, thank you.


01:00:53.886 --> 01:00:55.319
Your parents
are cool.


01:00:55.420 --> 01:00:58.048
Everyone says I'm gonna
hate them in a few years.


01:00:58.156 --> 01:01:00.420
Think you will?


01:01:00.526 --> 01:01:01.550
Probably.


01:01:01.660 --> 01:01:05.096
If people say so.


01:01:05.197 --> 01:01:06.755
This is the time.


01:01:06.865 --> 01:01:08.958
I know it. She knows it.


01:01:09.067 --> 01:01:11.228
My God,
even her parents know it.


01:01:11.336 --> 01:01:12.633
Why can't I kiss her?


01:01:12.738 --> 01:01:13.898
What's stopping me?


01:01:14.006 --> 01:01:15.633
Is it cooties I fear?


01:01:15.741 --> 01:01:18.642
So... big wedding
this weekend.


01:01:18.744 --> 01:01:20.177
Yeah, right.


01:01:20.279 --> 01:01:22.144
I forgot about that.


01:01:22.247 --> 01:01:25.410
I wish you could come.


01:01:25.517 --> 01:01:28.611
It's gonna be
really boring.


01:01:28.720 --> 01:01:30.551
Yeah, I really
wanna see you


01:01:30.656 --> 01:01:33.523
do your flower
girl thing.


01:01:33.625 --> 01:01:35.957
Part of me is sure
I'm gonna tr...


01:01:41.934 --> 01:01:43.993
Did... did I do it right?


01:01:46.038 --> 01:01:47.596
I don't know.


01:01:47.706 --> 01:01:50.106
I have absolutely
nothing to compare it to.


01:01:50.208 --> 01:01:51.800
My God, was I even close?


01:01:51.910 --> 01:01:52.968
I...


01:01:53.078 --> 01:01:55.376
I should go.


01:01:55.480 --> 01:01:57.471
Yeah.


01:01:59.484 --> 01:02:00.712
Good night.


01:02:00.819 --> 01:02:03.185
Good night.


01:02:12.397 --> 01:02:14.490
Hey, how was your night,
little Romeo?


01:02:14.600 --> 01:02:15.794
It was good.


01:02:15.901 --> 01:02:17.334
It was great.


01:02:17.436 --> 01:02:20.633
Fine, I think.


01:02:20.739 --> 01:02:23.674
But I had no idea.


01:02:23.775 --> 01:02:28.337
I kept playing the moment over
and over and over in my head.


01:02:28.447 --> 01:02:33.146
Was it too fast?
Too hard? Too gross?


01:02:33.251 --> 01:02:35.310
Did she actually
want me to kiss her?


01:02:35.420 --> 01:02:36.011
I gotta go.


01:02:36.121 --> 01:02:36.951
I gotta go.


01:02:37.055 --> 01:02:37.783
I gotta go.


01:02:37.889 --> 01:02:39.754
or did I scare her away?


01:02:39.858 --> 01:02:41.883
oh, I had it bad,
this new feeling...


01:02:41.994 --> 01:02:43.621
deep in the pit of my stomach.


01:02:43.729 --> 01:02:45.629
This horrible love sickness.


01:02:48.000 --> 01:02:49.194
( retching, vomiting )


01:02:49.301 --> 01:02:51.769
Maybe this is what cooties are.


01:02:51.870 --> 01:02:54.065
By the next day, I was a wreck.


01:02:54.172 --> 01:02:56.231
I purposely didn't call her-


01:02:56.341 --> 01:02:58.138
okay, except for one hang-up-


01:02:58.243 --> 01:03:00.370
because I knew
I would see her in karate.


01:03:00.479 --> 01:03:03.642
I got to class
ten minutes early.


01:03:07.285 --> 01:03:08.946
Hey.


01:03:09.054 --> 01:03:11.113
Hey.


01:03:11.223 --> 01:03:16.923
okay, I knew what I was doing
here early, but what was he?


01:03:17.029 --> 01:03:20.795
one thing was clear-
this business


01:03:20.899 --> 01:03:23.561
had to be settled
right here and right now.


01:03:23.669 --> 01:03:25.159
Staples.


01:03:46.825 --> 01:03:47.917
Ki-yah!


01:03:50.128 --> 01:03:51.095
Ki-yah!


01:03:53.432 --> 01:03:55.457
( grunting )


01:04:03.842 --> 01:04:05.173
Ki-yah!


01:04:05.277 --> 01:04:07.438
( mirror shattering )


01:04:11.249 --> 01:04:13.217
If only life was so simple.


01:04:13.318 --> 01:04:14.478
( sighs )


01:04:15.721 --> 01:04:17.621
3..09.
She's not even coming.


01:04:17.723 --> 01:04:18.690
TEACHER:
Hai.!


01:04:18.790 --> 01:04:20.781
She doesn't
even want to see me.


01:04:20.892 --> 01:04:22.450
She's blowing off class.


01:04:22.561 --> 01:04:23.789
She hates me.


01:04:23.895 --> 01:04:25.795
Your fists should
be like a hammer.


01:04:29.000 --> 01:04:31.400
She came.
She's here. She loves me.


01:04:31.503 --> 01:04:33.801
Sorry I'm late.


01:04:33.905 --> 01:04:36.169
TEACHER:
Miss Telesco, nice
of you to join us.


01:04:39.911 --> 01:04:41.378
Wait a minute.


01:04:41.480 --> 01:04:42.845
What was that?


01:04:42.948 --> 01:04:46.281
Was that a smile,
or is she, like, mad at me?


01:04:46.384 --> 01:04:49.820
Why would she be mad at me?
I only kissed her.


01:04:49.921 --> 01:04:52.151
Why the heck did I kiss her?


01:04:52.257 --> 01:04:54.725
What was I possibly thinking?


01:04:54.826 --> 01:04:55.815
Ki-yah!


01:04:58.130 --> 01:05:00.064
There are very few things
more painful


01:05:00.165 --> 01:05:03.999
than watching the woman you
love grapple with another man.


01:05:04.102 --> 01:05:06.093
Actually, I take that back.


01:05:06.204 --> 01:05:08.672
There are
no things more painful.


01:05:08.774 --> 01:05:10.674
The answer lies
within you, Gabriel...


01:05:10.776 --> 01:05:11.970
and you alone.


01:05:12.077 --> 01:05:13.635
You must find
your strength.


01:05:13.745 --> 01:05:16.908
Your focus.
Your determination.


01:05:17.015 --> 01:05:18.414
Ki-yah!


01:05:18.517 --> 01:05:19.609
Ki-yah!


01:05:19.718 --> 01:05:21.686
Ki-yah! Ki-yah! Ki-yah!


01:05:21.787 --> 01:05:23.755
Poor David Betanahu.


01:05:23.855 --> 01:05:26.016
He was an innocent victim
in all this.


01:05:26.124 --> 01:05:27.785
Collateral damage
in this love affair.


01:05:27.893 --> 01:05:31.989
one, two, three, four...


01:05:32.097 --> 01:05:34.031
I couldn't
take my eyes offher.


01:05:34.132 --> 01:05:35.497
- High block...
- She loves me.


01:05:35.600 --> 01:05:36.532
...middle punch,
Ki-yah!


01:05:36.635 --> 01:05:39.103
She loves me not.


01:05:39.204 --> 01:05:41.638
She loves me.


01:05:41.740 --> 01:05:43.105
Loves me not.


01:05:43.208 --> 01:05:45.870
She loves me. Not. Not.


01:05:45.977 --> 01:05:47.604
Loves. Not.


01:05:47.712 --> 01:05:52.172
By 3..5 1, I had descended
fully into madness.


01:05:52.284 --> 01:05:54.047
Who wants to take
their yellow belt exam?


01:05:54.152 --> 01:05:54.948
Me!


01:05:55.053 --> 01:05:56.645
( classmates gasping )


01:05:56.755 --> 01:05:58.120
Ah, Gabe.


01:05:58.223 --> 01:06:00.316
The moment
of reckoning is upon us.


01:06:00.425 --> 01:06:02.655
okay, maybe I was
a little overeager...


01:06:02.761 --> 01:06:04.661
but it was
my only way back to her.


01:06:04.763 --> 01:06:07.960
Luckily, I had the great master
of masters in my corner.


01:06:08.066 --> 01:06:09.226
Ki-yah!


01:06:09.334 --> 01:06:11.564
Ah, very nice. Very nice.


01:06:11.670 --> 01:06:13.160
Let's see your Mochizuki now.


01:06:13.271 --> 01:06:14.135
Hit, switch.


01:06:14.239 --> 01:06:16.070
Hit! Hit!
Sweep.


01:06:18.677 --> 01:06:19.871
oh...


01:06:19.978 --> 01:06:23.414
very nice, very nice.


01:06:23.515 --> 01:06:25.176
You've come a long way.


01:06:25.283 --> 01:06:28.480
Excellent Gabriel. Excellent.


01:06:28.587 --> 01:06:31.852
Now, time for the break.


01:06:31.957 --> 01:06:34.858
All that stood between me
and the woman I loved


01:06:34.960 --> 01:06:38.054
was a half-inch
piece of plywood.


01:06:38.163 --> 01:06:40.256
Be the board,
Gabe.


01:06:40.365 --> 01:06:41.889
Be the board.


01:06:44.035 --> 01:06:46.936
At that moment,
I was the board.


01:06:48.773 --> 01:06:50.070
Ki-yah!


01:06:52.310 --> 01:06:54.608
( groaning )


01:06:54.713 --> 01:06:57.409
( gasping, groaning )


01:06:57.515 --> 01:06:59.039
ow! ow!


01:06:59.150 --> 01:07:01.812
ow! oh! Aah...!


01:07:01.920 --> 01:07:05.378
( whimpering,
howling )


01:07:05.490 --> 01:07:06.855
The pain! The pain!


01:07:06.958 --> 01:07:08.186
oh, my God!


01:07:08.293 --> 01:07:10.284
ow!


01:07:10.395 --> 01:07:13.626
oh, ow... Aw...


01:07:13.732 --> 01:07:15.632
( groaning )


01:07:15.734 --> 01:07:18.396
( howling ):
ow...!


01:07:18.503 --> 01:07:21.131
I don't remember
much after that.


01:07:21.239 --> 01:07:22.206
Gabe...


01:07:22.307 --> 01:07:24.298
They, um, they said
I blacked out.


01:07:24.409 --> 01:07:25.343
( machine whirring quietly )


01:07:25.343 --> 01:07:26.810
( machine whirring quietly )


01:07:38.223 --> 01:07:39.781
( mouthing word )


01:07:42.560 --> 01:07:45.893
I guess this
is the end of karate, huh?


01:07:45.997 --> 01:07:48.727
( sighs ):
I'm a placekicker.


01:07:48.833 --> 01:07:51.028
If you work hard,
you can achieve anything.


01:07:51.136 --> 01:07:52.694
I really believe
that, Gabe.


01:07:52.804 --> 01:07:54.362
Whatever.


01:07:56.274 --> 01:07:57.298
- Hey.
- Hey.


01:07:57.409 --> 01:07:59.309
I came as soon
as I got the message.


01:07:59.411 --> 01:08:00.901
What happened?


01:08:01.012 --> 01:08:04.675
He went a little too hard
for his yellow belt.


01:08:04.783 --> 01:08:06.250
Mm.


01:08:06.351 --> 01:08:07.409
Sounds like
we're gonna need


01:08:07.519 --> 01:08:08.986
some ice cream on
the way home, huh?


01:08:09.087 --> 01:08:11.920
No, thanks.


01:08:14.259 --> 01:08:16.250
Was this it?


01:08:16.361 --> 01:08:18.761
Was this the end
for me and Rosemary?


01:08:18.863 --> 01:08:21.161
Two and a half weeks
was all the time


01:08:21.266 --> 01:08:22.756
we were going to be allowed?


01:08:22.867 --> 01:08:24.357
I was not gonna call her.


01:08:24.469 --> 01:08:26.198
That would be weak.


01:08:26.304 --> 01:08:28.829
And I resolved that night
to be weak no longer.


01:08:28.940 --> 01:08:31.033
- ( phone rings )
- Hello?


01:08:31.142 --> 01:08:33.474
Hello, Mrs. Burton?


01:08:33.578 --> 01:08:35.136
No, this is Gabe.


01:08:35.246 --> 01:08:38.113
Who cares if she thought
I was my mother? It was her.!


01:08:38.216 --> 01:08:40.116
Hello?


01:08:40.218 --> 01:08:41.378
No, Mom, I got it.


01:08:41.486 --> 01:08:42.418
Who is it?


01:08:42.520 --> 01:08:44.112
Mom, I got it.
Hang up now.


01:08:44.222 --> 01:08:45.154
okay, hon.


01:08:45.256 --> 01:08:46.655
Hey.


01:08:46.758 --> 01:08:49.625
Hey, how's your hand?


01:08:49.728 --> 01:08:50.695
My hand?


01:08:50.795 --> 01:08:52.228
oh, it's fine. Barely hurt.


01:08:52.330 --> 01:08:55.231
I just got so worried
when you lost consciousness.


01:08:55.333 --> 01:08:58.496
Yeah, that was only,
like, for a second or so.


01:08:58.603 --> 01:09:00.230
What color cast did you get?


01:09:00.338 --> 01:09:02.499
Plain was the best
of my choices.


01:09:02.607 --> 01:09:05.201
My cousin got this Hulk one.


01:09:05.310 --> 01:09:08.507
Yeah, they had that, too, but
I'm not really into the Hulk.


01:09:08.613 --> 01:09:10.376
This was
no time for small talk.


01:09:10.482 --> 01:09:12.382
It was time
to lay things on the table.


01:09:12.484 --> 01:09:13.917
To reach
through that phone line


01:09:14.019 --> 01:09:15.816
and dig deep
into that woman's soul.


01:09:15.920 --> 01:09:18.821
So when can we hang out?


01:09:18.923 --> 01:09:22.256
It's a really
crazy weekend for me.


01:09:22.360 --> 01:09:23.520
It is?


01:09:23.628 --> 01:09:24.788
It's Thursday night.


01:09:24.896 --> 01:09:26.420
She's going to camp
Sunday morning.


01:09:26.531 --> 01:09:28.294
Who cares how crazy
the weekend is?


01:09:28.400 --> 01:09:29.492
Rehearsal dinner tomorrow night...


01:09:29.601 --> 01:09:32.764
wedding on Saturday,
camp on Sunday.


01:09:32.871 --> 01:09:34.839
Sure, right. of course.


01:09:34.939 --> 01:09:37.430
Where's her whole ""Wish you
could come to the wedding'?


01:09:37.542 --> 01:09:39.806
Where's that Rosemary?
The Rosemary I loved.


01:09:39.911 --> 01:09:42.345
Not this alien
with her crazy weekends.


01:09:42.447 --> 01:09:44.881
Your new sparring partner,
is he coming to the wedding?


01:09:44.983 --> 01:09:46.848
What? Tim?


01:09:46.951 --> 01:09:48.043
oh, is that what you call him?


01:09:48.153 --> 01:09:50.121
Are you calling him
after you call me?


01:09:50.221 --> 01:09:51.813
What are you talking about?


01:09:51.923 --> 01:09:54.551
I'm talking about you and
Tim Staples sitting in a tree.


01:09:54.659 --> 01:09:56.627
K-I-S-S-I-N-G


01:09:56.728 --> 01:09:57.990
First comes love


01:09:58.096 --> 01:09:59.256
Then comes marriage


01:09:59.364 --> 01:10:01.559
Then comes Tim Staples
in a baby carriage.


01:10:01.666 --> 01:10:03.190
You sound crazy, you know that?


01:10:03.301 --> 01:10:05.064
Why don't you
have time this weekend?


01:10:05.170 --> 01:10:08.401
I'm sorry, Gabe.
I haven't even started packing.


01:10:08.506 --> 01:10:09.768
You know what? I hate you.


01:10:09.874 --> 01:10:11.432
What?!


01:10:11.543 --> 01:10:13.443
I hate you.
Why do you even care?


01:10:13.545 --> 01:10:14.477
I hate you.


01:10:14.579 --> 01:10:16.046
Well, I hate you, too.


01:10:16.147 --> 01:10:17.273
I hate you more.


01:10:17.382 --> 01:10:19.873
How can you
say something so mean?


01:10:19.984 --> 01:10:21.474
I hate you!


01:10:21.586 --> 01:10:22.746
( slams receiver )


01:10:24.856 --> 01:10:26.187
( receiver slams )


01:10:31.362 --> 01:10:33.091
( crying )


01:10:37.802 --> 01:10:39.292
Rosemary!


01:10:48.079 --> 01:10:49.944
Rosemary!


01:11:00.225 --> 01:11:02.625
You want to or should I?


01:11:07.132 --> 01:11:10.124
Rosemary!


01:11:10.235 --> 01:11:12.362
It was the pain
that had no name.


01:11:12.470 --> 01:11:15.234
oh! ooh! ow! ow! ow!


01:11:17.041 --> 01:11:20.875
Why did Rosemary Telesco
ever have to walk into my life?


01:11:20.979 --> 01:11:23.311
Why, why, why?


01:11:28.219 --> 01:11:33.486
Maybe not everything
is supposed to last forever.


01:11:33.591 --> 01:11:39.154
Certain things are like...
like... skywriting.


01:11:39.264 --> 01:11:41.664
Like, like, like
a really beautiful thing


01:11:41.766 --> 01:11:44.530
that lasts for
a couple moments and then...


01:11:44.636 --> 01:11:45.568
You know?


01:11:45.670 --> 01:11:47.194
( crying )


01:11:54.245 --> 01:11:55.337
Mommy!


01:11:55.446 --> 01:11:57.676
I know, honey.


01:11:57.782 --> 01:11:59.841
Love sucks.


01:11:59.951 --> 01:12:01.009
Yeah.


01:12:08.726 --> 01:12:09.818
Look at them all.


01:12:09.928 --> 01:12:12.089
Rats in their cages...


01:12:12.197 --> 01:12:14.893
their lives destroyed by love.


01:12:14.999 --> 01:12:16.023
I'm done with it.


01:12:18.102 --> 01:12:20.297
I won't be like them.


01:12:20.405 --> 01:12:21.838
( grunts )


01:12:21.940 --> 01:12:23.601
The fools.


01:12:27.212 --> 01:12:29.077
I remember
my first girl.


01:12:29.180 --> 01:12:30.169
We met on
theJersey shore.


01:12:30.281 --> 01:12:31.270
She was from Philly...


01:12:31.382 --> 01:12:32.542
I was from Brooklyn...


01:12:32.650 --> 01:12:35.141
so, we knew right from
the start, we were cursed.


01:12:35.253 --> 01:12:37.187
Ralph, not right now.
I'm not in the mood.


01:12:37.288 --> 01:12:38.915
okay.


01:12:42.460 --> 01:12:45.987
oh, hejsan.
God morgon.


01:12:46.097 --> 01:12:47.223
Hejsan.


01:13:10.555 --> 01:13:16.016
( alternative )


01:13:33.077 --> 01:13:38.447
( continues )


01:13:47.625 --> 01:13:50.253
It's amazing how quickly
time moves.


01:13:50.361 --> 01:13:53.387
just yesterday,
I thought I loved her.


01:13:53.498 --> 01:13:56.729
But now I don't even
care about her at all.


01:13:56.834 --> 01:14:00.463
( continues )


01:14:11.582 --> 01:14:14.346
( song ends )


01:14:15.720 --> 01:14:21.158
The next morning, this kind
of amazing thing happened.


01:14:21.259 --> 01:14:23.921
The sun came out again.


01:14:24.028 --> 01:14:27.020
See, life is about so much more
than Rosemary.


01:14:27.131 --> 01:14:32.569
I have my family, my health,
my kicking career.


01:14:32.670 --> 01:14:35.935
I really had no room
for a woman in my life.


01:14:36.040 --> 01:14:39.066
How about some rocky road?


01:14:39.177 --> 01:14:41.441
I guess.


01:14:45.183 --> 01:14:46.343
Dad?


01:14:46.451 --> 01:14:47.884
Yeah.


01:14:47.985 --> 01:14:50.180
What's the deal
with girls?


01:14:50.288 --> 01:14:52.381
I mean, why are they
the way they are?


01:14:56.327 --> 01:14:58.488
You're talking
to the wrong man.


01:14:59.564 --> 01:15:03.398
Well, how come all love
has to end?


01:15:13.177 --> 01:15:19.082
Let me... let me tell you
something about me and your mom.


01:15:19.183 --> 01:15:23.711
once upon a time,
we really loved each other.


01:15:23.821 --> 01:15:27.348
But as... as time went by...


01:15:27.458 --> 01:15:30.552
there just got to be
all these... these things-


01:15:30.661 --> 01:15:32.026
little things...


01:15:32.130 --> 01:15:35.566
stupid things that
were left unsaid.


01:15:35.666 --> 01:15:37.793
And all these things
that were left unsaid


01:15:37.902 --> 01:15:42.362
piled up like... like
the clutter in our storage room.


01:15:42.473 --> 01:15:44.373
And after awhile...


01:15:44.475 --> 01:15:46.340
there was so much
that was left unsaid...


01:15:46.444 --> 01:15:50.141
that we barely said anything
at all.


01:15:50.248 --> 01:15:54.150
Well... why didn't you
just say 'em then, Dad?


01:15:57.021 --> 01:16:00.149
I don't know, Gabe.


01:16:00.258 --> 01:16:02.283
I kinda wish I had.


01:16:04.061 --> 01:16:05.494
Who was I kidding, anyway?


01:16:05.596 --> 01:16:07.689
I wasn't going to get
any real comfort here.


01:16:07.799 --> 01:16:10.597
I mean, the old guy
meant okay.


01:16:10.701 --> 01:16:12.965
Let's knock over a hot dog stand
on the way home.


01:16:13.070 --> 01:16:16.403
Drown our sorrows in pork
shoulders and nitrates.


01:16:16.507 --> 01:16:17.997
Nah, I think it's all right.


01:16:18.109 --> 01:16:21.010
I'm just going to, I don't know,
hang out here for awhile.


01:16:21.112 --> 01:16:23.580
okay, champ.


01:16:23.681 --> 01:16:25.012
See you
at the homestead.


01:16:25.116 --> 01:16:26.014
All right.


01:16:26.117 --> 01:16:27.516
You kicked good today.


01:16:27.618 --> 01:16:30.052
I'm telling you,
the trajectory you're on-


01:16:30.154 --> 01:16:31.553
to the moon.


01:16:31.656 --> 01:16:32.816
or at least the Big Ten.


01:16:32.924 --> 01:16:34.414
Thanks.


01:16:34.525 --> 01:16:36.049
Felt good.


01:16:36.160 --> 01:16:38.720
Good. I'll see
you at home.


01:16:43.301 --> 01:16:45.496
Somewhere,
a million miles away...


01:16:45.603 --> 01:16:51.701
the girl I once loved
was going down her road...


01:16:51.809 --> 01:16:53.743
and I was stuck back on mine.


01:17:40.358 --> 01:17:41.950
I couldn't escape them-


01:17:42.059 --> 01:17:45.051
all the little things
I left unsaid.


01:17:45.162 --> 01:17:47.858
I was drowning in them.


01:18:01.646 --> 01:18:04.206
Suddenly,
I knew what I had to do.


01:18:06.284 --> 01:18:08.650
Love isn't about ridiculous
little words.


01:18:08.753 --> 01:18:10.084
Love is about grand gestures.


01:18:10.187 --> 01:18:13.213
Don't go to Taos,
not without me.


01:18:13.324 --> 01:18:17.192
Love is about airplanes
pulling banners over stadiums.


01:18:17.295 --> 01:18:19.559
Proposals on Jumbotrons.


01:18:19.664 --> 01:18:22.792
Giant words in skywriting.


01:18:22.900 --> 01:18:26.563
Love is about going that
extra mile, even if it hurts.


01:18:26.671 --> 01:18:31.040
Letting it all hang out there.


01:18:31.142 --> 01:18:32.609
Love is about fiinding courage
inside of you


01:18:32.710 --> 01:18:35.611
that you didn't even know
was there.


01:18:59.804 --> 01:19:06.232
( jazz standard )


01:19:28.599 --> 01:19:30.692
( continues )


01:19:30.801 --> 01:19:31.768
Whew.


01:20:03.868 --> 01:20:07.599
( song fades )


01:20:07.705 --> 01:20:09.832
What are you
doing here?


01:20:09.940 --> 01:20:11.532
You're going to
camp tomorrow.


01:20:11.642 --> 01:20:13.507
I had to say good-bye.


01:20:13.611 --> 01:20:16.637
But I thought you hate me.


01:20:16.747 --> 01:20:18.942
I don't.


01:20:19.050 --> 01:20:20.642
I lied.


01:20:20.751 --> 01:20:22.685
I wasn't going
to be like my father.


01:20:22.787 --> 01:20:27.747
I wasn't going to let all these
things left unsaid smother me.


01:20:27.858 --> 01:20:29.450
Rosemary...


01:20:32.430 --> 01:20:35.661
I love you.


01:20:35.766 --> 01:20:37.927
You what?


01:20:38.035 --> 01:20:39.434
I do.


01:20:39.537 --> 01:20:41.232
I'm sorry...


01:20:41.338 --> 01:20:43.932
but I love you more than anyone
has ever loved.


01:20:44.041 --> 01:20:46.009
I love you, I love you,
I love you.


01:20:46.110 --> 01:20:48.271
How's that for letting it
all hang out there...


01:20:48.379 --> 01:20:56.047
and hang and hang and hang?


01:20:56.153 --> 01:20:59.281
Do you, um...


01:20:59.390 --> 01:21:02.086
you think you might
want to love me, too?


01:21:02.193 --> 01:21:04.855
I don't know
what I think, Gabe.


01:21:04.962 --> 01:21:09.490
I'm only 1 1 .


01:21:09.600 --> 01:21:13.127
I don't think
I'm ready to be in love.


01:21:13.237 --> 01:21:15.797
I'm not ready,
and I'm doing it.


01:21:15.906 --> 01:21:17.840
But it wasn't that easy.


01:21:17.942 --> 01:21:19.705
I guess love never is.


01:21:19.810 --> 01:21:22.677
Maybe I was wrong.


01:21:22.780 --> 01:21:25.044
Maybe... maybe girls
don't mature faster.


01:21:25.149 --> 01:21:26.116
No, they do...


01:21:26.217 --> 01:21:28.082
they do,
you know they do.


01:21:28.185 --> 01:21:30.153
You even said so at the park.


01:21:30.254 --> 01:21:32.154
We at least mature
at the same rate.


01:21:34.158 --> 01:21:35.989
I don't know
what mature is anymore.


01:21:40.364 --> 01:21:44.164
But I'm really happy you came.


01:21:50.074 --> 01:21:52.736
Do you want
to dance, Gabe?


01:21:52.843 --> 01:21:53.810
Dance?


01:21:55.146 --> 01:21:57.979
Sure, what the hell?


01:22:02.019 --> 01:22:09.755
( jazz ballad )


01:22:11.962 --> 01:22:15.193
As I held onto Rosemary
Telesco for dear life...


01:22:15.299 --> 01:22:17.426
we both knew the truth.


01:22:17.535 --> 01:22:19.765
She was going off to camp...


01:22:19.870 --> 01:22:22.532
and eventually, private school.


01:22:22.640 --> 01:22:24.938
We were on different roads,
she and me.


01:22:25.042 --> 01:22:27.977
Two ships that passed
in Sheep Meadow.


01:22:37.154 --> 01:22:38.883
( continues )


01:22:40.090 --> 01:22:42.422
See, this is just like
I told you.


01:22:42.526 --> 01:22:45.120
Same thing I knew
getting into this whole mess..


01:22:45.229 --> 01:22:48.756
Love ends.


01:22:51.068 --> 01:22:52.968
Hey, Mr. Gabe.
How goes it?


01:22:53.070 --> 01:22:54.230
Hey, Ralph.


01:22:54.338 --> 01:22:55.703
WoMAN:
Hold the door, please.


01:22:55.806 --> 01:22:58.900
( woman laughing )


01:23:00.978 --> 01:23:04.414
( song ends )


01:23:05.950 --> 01:23:10.046
The truth is,
you come into this world alone


01:23:10.154 --> 01:23:13.282
and leave it
the exact same way.


01:23:13.390 --> 01:23:15.483
Home.


01:23:38.282 --> 01:23:41.149
( laughing in distance )


01:23:47.191 --> 01:23:49.455
( laughter )


01:23:54.531 --> 01:23:57.125
( laughter continues )


01:24:04.408 --> 01:24:05.875
Who are these strangers...


01:24:05.976 --> 01:24:08.103
laughing in
my mother's bedroom?


01:24:08.212 --> 01:24:10.737
I've only seen them
in pictures.


01:24:10.848 --> 01:24:12.475
Hi.


01:24:12.583 --> 01:24:15.552
( laughing )


01:24:15.653 --> 01:24:18.816
Um, everything okay?


01:24:18.923 --> 01:24:20.356
Yeah.
We were just talking


01:24:20.457 --> 01:24:23.551
about how horrible
our honeymoon was.


01:24:23.661 --> 01:24:25.128
( chuckles ):
Yeah?


01:24:25.229 --> 01:24:26.457
Key West.


01:24:26.563 --> 01:24:29.589
Everything that could
possibly go wrong...


01:24:29.700 --> 01:24:31.133
An unmitigated disaster.


01:24:31.235 --> 01:24:33.430
It wasn't even a tropical storm.
Remember that?


01:24:33.537 --> 01:24:35.937
- Like yesterday.
- It was awful.


01:24:36.040 --> 01:24:37.200
We lost our luggage.


01:24:37.308 --> 01:24:38.741
God, you were so sick.


01:24:38.842 --> 01:24:40.571
( both groan )


01:24:40.678 --> 01:24:42.669
God, I'm hungry.
What time is it?


01:24:42.780 --> 01:24:44.270
oh, wow.


01:24:44.381 --> 01:24:46.349
We should get
something to eat.


01:24:46.450 --> 01:24:49.248
All of us?


01:24:49.353 --> 01:24:51.947
Yeah. We should, uh...


01:24:52.056 --> 01:24:55.048
Why don't we go down
to the place on the corner?


01:24:55.159 --> 01:24:56.251
GABE:
Yeah.


01:24:56.360 --> 01:24:58.328
Place on the corner
sounds good.


01:24:58.429 --> 01:25:00.158
ADAM:
It's getting cooler.


01:25:00.264 --> 01:25:03.028
Yeah, we're gonna
need jackets.


01:25:11.809 --> 01:25:13.436
I just cleared
some old stuff


01:25:13.544 --> 01:25:15.512
out of the storage room.


01:25:15.612 --> 01:25:18.672
( intro to ""In My Life'plays )


01:25:24.054 --> 01:25:28.855
( pop )


01:25:37.034 --> 01:25:39.628
You wanted a New York
love story?


01:25:39.737 --> 01:25:42.433
There's a New York love story
for ya.


01:25:42.539 --> 01:25:44.530
I told you
it wasn't gonna be pretty.


01:25:44.641 --> 01:25:46.734
( continues )


01:25:46.844 --> 01:25:49.074
Love is an ugly,
terrible business...


01:25:49.179 --> 01:25:50.441
practiced by fools.


01:25:50.547 --> 01:25:51.605
( Leslie laughs )


01:25:51.715 --> 01:25:52.739
It'll trample your heart


01:25:52.850 --> 01:25:55.045
and leave you bleeding
on the floor.


01:25:55.152 --> 01:25:58.485
And what does it really get you
in the end?


01:25:58.589 --> 01:26:00.955
Nothing but a few
incredible memories


01:26:01.058 --> 01:26:02.719
that you can't ever shake.


01:26:02.826 --> 01:26:04.418
- Whoa!
- Whoa!


01:26:05.996 --> 01:26:09.488
( continues )


01:26:09.600 --> 01:26:10.658
( thud )


01:26:10.768 --> 01:26:12.065
The truth is...


01:26:12.169 --> 01:26:14.296
there's gonna be other girls
out there.


01:26:14.405 --> 01:26:15.531
I mean...


01:26:15.639 --> 01:26:16.697
I hope.


01:26:16.807 --> 01:26:18.638
( continues )


01:26:18.742 --> 01:26:22.007
But I'm never gonna get
another fiirst love.


01:26:24.214 --> 01:26:25.875
That one's always gonna be her.


01:26:25.983 --> 01:26:28.508
( continues )


01:26:48.672 --> 01:26:50.663
( song ends )


01:26:55.045 --> 01:26:57.172
( alternative )


01:27:25.175 --> 01:27:28.702
( continues )


01:28:15.359 --> 01:28:17.190
( song ends )


01:28:21.031 --> 01:28:23.522
( new song, alternative )


01:28:56.967 --> 01:29:02.371
( continues )


01:30:01.265 --> 01:30:03.233
( music ends )


01:30:04.265 --> 01:30:08.233
